t["subzone:lakeridge-highway"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,320,15.451.0,17.420.0,38.189.0,29.249.0,35.187.0,33.181.0",["h"]="e19565",["n"]="Camino del Lago",["s"]="Camino del Lago. El Camino del Lago es una antigua vía que discurre a lo largo de la orilla sur del Lago Sempiterno, en las Montañas Crestagrana. Antaño una arteria vital y muy transitada antes de la Primera Guerra, ha caído en la ruina y el desuso. En la actualidad, manadas errantes de gnolls y orcos Roca Negra hacen que transitar por el camino sea peligroso para los viajeros. Antes de la devastación de la Primera Guerra, el Camino del Lago servía como un bullicioso corredor comercial a través de Crestagrana, transportando mercancías y gentes por la orilla sur del Lago Sempiterno. En aquellos días de paz, los viajeros podían desplazarse entre los asentamientos del valle y las colinas orientales bajo la protección del Reino de Ventormenta. Esa seguridad se hizo añicos cuando la Horda marchó por la región, dejando el este de Crestagrana disputado y desolado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The highway is a visible reminder of Stormwind's neglected frontiers, where local roads just outside Lakeshire have been surrendered to gnolls and orcs due to a lack of reinforcements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The road tracks along the southern edge of Lake Everstill, heading eastward out of the Lakeshire area toward the foothills surrounding Stonewatch Keep and the eastern mountains of Redridge.",["al"]={"where does lakeridge highway go","lakeridge highway path","where is lakeridge highway"},["q"]="Where does the Lakeridge Highway lead?"},{["a"]="The highway fell into disuse after the First War, particularly when Blackrock orcs fortified Stonewatch Keep. Without the manpower to secure the road, Stormwind could not maintain it, allowing hostile gnolls to move in and choke off civilian travel.",["al"]={"why is it abandoned","why is lakeridge highway empty","lakeridge highway fallen into disuse"},["q"]="Why is the highway abandoned?"},{["a"]="The highway is primarily haunted by aggressive gnolls that ambush anyone wandering away from Lakeshire, as well as lingering Blackrock orc scouts operating out of the eastern strongholds.",["al"]={"dangers on lakeridge highway","mobs on lakeridge highway","who controls lakeridge highway"},["q"]="What threats wander the road today?"},{["a"]="No. In the peaceful era before the First War, the Lakeridge Highway was a well-maintained, highly traveled route that safely connected the heart of Redridge to its eastern outposts.",["al"]={"lakeridge highway history","highway before the war"},["q"]="Was the highway always dangerous?"}},["kw"]={"gnolls","highway","lake everstill","lakeridge","redridge","road","stonewatch"},["n"]="Lakeridge Highway",["s"]="Lakeridge Highway is an old thoroughfare running along the southern shore of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. Once a vital and heavily traveled artery prior to the First War, it has fallen into ruin and disuse. Today, roving packs of gnolls and Blackrock orcs make passage along the road perilous for travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the devastation of the First War, the Lakeridge Highway served as a bustling trade corridor through Redridge, carrying goods and folk along the southern banks of Lake Everstill. In those peaceful days, travelers could journey between the valley settlements and the eastern heights under the protection of the Kingdom of Stormwind. That safety shattered when the Horde marched through the region, leaving eastern Redridge contested and desolate.",["t"]="A Fallen Artery"},{["b"]="Following the seizure of Stonewatch Keep by Blackrock orcs, regular maintenance and patrols along the highway ceased entirely. The road quickly deteriorated into an overgrown track contested by savage gnoll packs. With Stormwind's military spread thin and unable to reinforce Lakeshire, the highway remains officially unsafe. Any traveler seeking to reach the eastern ridges must now carve a path through gnoll ambushes.",["t"]="Peril on the Road"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeshire-inn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,263,18.532.0,20.514.0,45.203.0,53.255.0,23.229.0,42.161.0",["h"]="07ccf1",["n"]="posada de Villa del Lago",["s"]="posada de Villa del Lago. La posada de Villa del Lago es el centro social y el principal refugio del asediado pueblo de Villa del Lago. Situada en el corazón de las Montañas Crestagrana, ofrece calidez, cerveza y un alojamiento seguro tanto para los lugareños como para los cansados viajeros que se enfrentan a los peligros de los alrededores. Emplazada a orillas del Lago Sempiterno, la posada de Villa del Lago brinda un breve respiro frente a las bandas de gnolls y orcos Roca Negra que acosan al pueblo. A pesar de la situación militar cada vez más desesperada de Villa del Lago, la taberna conserva un ambiente acogedor y animado. El Posadero Daniels y la tabernera Brianna atienden a vecinos y viajeros, sirviendo jarras de cerveza, vino y platos calientes. Es un punto de encuentro vital donde la gente del pueblo intercambia noticias, ahoga sus penas y busca mercenarios que ayuden a defender la frontera oriental del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Lakeshire Inn is an indispensable stronghold of Alliance hospitality, serving as the staging ground for anyone fighting to protect Stormwind's vulnerable eastern flank.",["profession:Cooking"]="The common room is a lively spot to procure culinary staples, local recipes, and fresh drink from Barkeep Daniels while traveling through the mountains."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The inn functions as the primary rest stop in Redridge. Innkeeper Brianna binds hearthstones and rents rooms to weary travelers, while Barkeep Daniels supplies refreshments, food, and drink for the road.",["al"]={"lakeshire inn services","what can I do at lakeshire inn","innkeeper lakeshire"},["q"]="What services does the Lakeshire Inn provide?"},{["a"]="With orcs from the Blackrock clan descending from the northern crags and gnolls raiding local farms, townspeople and displaced settlers seek safety within the town center. The tavern provides both physical shelter and a place to share news of the defense.",["al"]={"why is lakeshire inn full","lakeshire refugees inn","redridge tavern crowd"},["q"]="Why is the inn so crowded despite the nearby attacks?"},{["a"]="Wiley the Black is a somber local figure found seated inside the inn. He keeps a sharp eye on the threats facing Lakeshire and provides insight and tasks to capable adventurers looking to push back the enemy presence in Redridge.",["al"]={"wiley the black","guy in lakeshire tavern","wiley npc"},["q"]="Who is Wiley the Black?"},{["a"]="The inn sits right near the western entrance of Lakeshire along the northern bank of Lake Everstill, just off the main road leading into town from Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"where is lakeshire inn","lakeshire tavern location","find lakeshire inn"},["q"]="Where is the inn located within Lakeshire?"}},["kw"]={"barkeep daniels","darcy parker","innkeeper brianna","lake everstill","lakeshire inn","redridge inn","wiley the black","yorus barleybrew"},["n"]="Lakeshire Inn",["s"]="The Lakeshire Inn is the social hub and primary refuge in the beleaguered town of Lakeshire. Situated in the heart of the Redridge Mountains, it provides warmth, ale, and safe lodging for local townsfolk and weary travelers contending with the surrounding perils.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the shore of Lake Everstill, the Lakeshire Inn offers a brief respite from the gnoll bands and Blackrock orcs pressing in on the town. Despite Lakeshire's increasingly desperate military situation, the tavern maintains a cozy, bustling atmosphere. Barkeep Daniels and Innkeeper Brianna attend to the locals and travelers, serving up flagons of ale, wine, and warm meals. It is a vital meeting point where townspeople trade news, drown their sorrows, and seek hired blades to help defend the eastern border of the kingdom.",["t"]="A Beacon of Warmth"},{["b"]="Beyond ordinary patrons nursing drinks at the counter, the inn draws a variety of colorful figures. Wiley the Black watches the room from a table, keeping his own counsel and keeping tabs on regional dangers. Traveling brewers like Yorus Barleybrew make stops here, while Darcy Parker and other townsfolk frequent the common room. For adventurers venturing further into the jagged peaks or heading south toward Duskwood, the inn is the final bastion of civilization and safety before entering contested wilderness.",["t"]="Patrons and Whispers"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeshire-town-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,255,27.550.0,27.207.0,40.183.0,50.234.0,44.141.0,46.170.0",["h"]="167b20",["n"]="ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago",["s"]="ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago. ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago sirve como sede administrativa de las Montañas Crestagrana, erigiéndose en el corazón del asentamiento junto al lago. En su interior, el Magistrado Salomón supervisa el gobierno local mientras lidia con las incesantes amenazas de los orcos Roca Negra y los gnolls. ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago es una envejecida estructura de piedra que ha sido reformada con esmero en múltiples ocasiones a lo largo de los años. Situada de forma prominente en Villa del Lago, alberga al Magistrado Salomón, un líder civil amable y dedicado con la tarea de mantener el orden en los confines orientales del Reino de Ventormenta. Con los recursos militares de Ventormenta al límite y la ayuda real siendo escasa, el ayuntamiento ha pasado de ser una tranquila oficina administrativa a un activo centro de mando donde se tramitan a diario peticiones desesperadas de defensores voluntarios y mercenarios.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire Town Hall represents the eastern frontier of the Alliance in Redridge, standing as a beleaguered outpost desperately holding the line without royal support from Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, this refurbished hall reflects both the enduring spirit of rural settlements and the frustrating abandonment felt by regional administrators when the capital turns a blind eye."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magistrate Solomon oversees the town hall. He is a kind and well-meaning administrator who serves as the primary governing authority for Lakeshire and the surrounding Redridge valley.",["al"]={"who leads lakeshire","magistrate solomon","who is in town hall"},["q"]="Who is in charge at Lakeshire Town Hall?"},{["a"]="Lakeshire faces severe, mounting threats from local gnoll packs and hostile Blackrock orc warbands. Because Stormwind has provided minimal military reinforcements, Magistrate Solomon must hire passing adventurers to defend the region.",["al"]={"why does solomon need help","lakeshire problems","why are there so many quests here"},["q"]="Why is the town hall seeking so much outside help?"},{["a"]="The town's problems with gnolls and Blackrock orcs have put Solomon in a desperate position. He readily accepts aid from helpful adventurers.",["al"]={"why does solomon accept aid","lakeshire adventurers","town hall help"},["q"]="Why does Solomon accept help from travelers?"},{["a"]="Yes, it is an older building that has survived turbulent decades and undergone diligent repairs and refurbishments to keep it functioning as the civic center of Redridge.",["al"]={"town hall age","how old is lakeshire town hall","town hall history"},["q"]="Has Lakeshire Town Hall stood for a long time?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock","gnolls","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","redridge mountains","stormwind","town hall"},["n"]="Lakeshire Town Hall",["s"]="Lakeshire Town Hall serves as the administrative seat of the Redridge Mountains, standing at the heart of the lakeside settlement. Inside, Magistrate Solomon oversees local governance while wrestling with relentless threats from Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Lakeshire Town Hall is an aging stone structure that has been diligently refurbished multiple times over the years. Positioned prominently within Lakeshire, it houses Magistrate Solomon, a kind and dedicated civil leader tasked with maintaining order in the eastern reaches of the Kingdom of Stormwind. With Stormwind's military resources stretched thin and royal aid scarce, the hall has transformed from a quiet administrative office into an active command center where desperate appeals for volunteer defenders and mercenaries are processed daily.",["t"]="Seat of Redridge Governance"},{["b"]="Gnoll incursions and the encroaching Blackrock orcs have pushed Solomon to desperation. With aid scarce, the magistrate readily accepts help from independent adventurers who come through the town hall doors.",["t"]="Under Siege and Overwhelmed"}}}}}
t["subzone:longshore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,255,23.513.0,34.260.0,23.284.0,44.239.0,34.262.0",["h"]="0e8ae3",["n"]="Playa Larga",["s"]="Playa Larga. Playa Larga es la amplia costa arenosa que se extiende a lo largo de todo el límite occidental de Páramos de Poniente. A pesar de su vasta y pintoresca extensión, la orilla es célebremente peligrosa debido a las densas poblaciones de múrlocs agresivos y a los naufragios dispersos frente a la costa. A lo largo de todo el extremo occidental de Páramos de Poniente, Playa Larga es una de las playas continuas más extensas de los Reinos del Este. Sin embargo, ofrece poca paz a los viajeros. Los múrlocs costeros dominan el oleaje, liderados por notorios terrores como el Viejo Ojosombrío, mientras que los restos de navíos hundidos —incluidos destructores élficos en ruinas— salpican las aguas poco profundas. Cerca de los confines meridionales, colonos aislados como Daphne Fontana luchan contra los bandidos saqueadores de los Defias, a la vista del Faro de Poniente al otro lado del agua.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Alliance druids must brave the depths off the northwestern Longshore, locating a lockbox hidden near a sunken wreck to assemble the pendant required for their aquatic form.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins following the guidance of Duthorian Rall in Stormwind are sent south to Daphne Stilwell's homestead on Longshore, proving their valor by shielding an innocent farmer from Defias raiders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shoreline is infested with aggressive murloc tribes that roam unchecked across the sands, ambushing anyone who strays too close to the surf. In addition to the murlocs, the southern end of the beach is troubled by Defias bandits raiding coastal homesteads.",["al"]={"why are there so many murlocs","longshore hazards","is longshore safe"},["q"]="Why is the Longshore so dangerous?"},{["a"]="Daphne Stilwell is a lone settler maintaining an isolated farm on the southwestern stretch of the Longshore. Her vulnerable position makes her a frequent target for raids by the Defias Brotherhood, prompting the Knights of the Silver Hand to dispatch paladin initiates to her defense.",["al"]={"daphne stilwell","stilwell farm","woman on the beach"},["q"]="Who is Daphne Stilwell?"},{["a"]="Numerous wrecks lie submerged off the Longshore, ranging from merchant vessels to elven destroyers lost during past naval conflicts. These underwater ruins attract scavengers, murlocs, and adventurers seeking relics lost beneath the waves.",["al"]={"elven destroyers westfall","sunken ships longshore","shipwrecks"},["q"]="What are the shipwrecks lying off the coast?"},{["a"]="Alliance druids undertake a rite known as the Trial of the Sea Lion to master their aquatic form. Part of this trial requires seeking out a submerged chest near an offshore shipwreck along northwestern Longshore to retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance.",["al"]={"druid quest longshore","strange lockbox westfall","half pendant of aquatic endurance"},["q"]="Why do druids visit the Longshore?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","daphne stilwell","longshore","murloc","old murk-eye","shipwrecks","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},["n"]="Longshore",["s"]="The Longshore is the expansive sandy coastline stretching along the entire western edge of Westfall. Despite its vast and scenic expanse, the shore is notoriously hazardous due to thick populations of aggressive murlocs and scattered wrecks off the coast.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running the full western length of Westfall, the Longshore is one of the widest unbroken beaches in the Eastern Kingdoms. Yet it offers little peace to travelers. Coastal murlocs dominate the surf, led by notorious terrors like Old Murk-Eye, while the remnants of sunken vessels—including ruined elven destroyers—litter the shallows. Near the southern reaches, isolated settlers like Daphne Stilwell struggle against marauding Defias bandits, standing within sight of the Westfall Lighthouse across the water.",["t"]="A Treacherous Coastline"}}}}}
t["subzone:lordamere-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,349,28.598.0,19.525.0,51.222.0,51.207.0,27.184.0,30.150.0",["h"]="62ed52",["n"]="Lago Lordamere",["s"]="Lago Lordamere. El Lago Lordamere es una de las mayores masas de agua dulce de los Reinos del Este, bordeada por los Claros de Tirisfal, el Bosque de Argénteos y las Montañas de Alterac. En su día fue el bullicioso corazón acuático de la civilización humana en el norte, pero sus frías aguas e islas están ahora atormentadas por nigromantes de la Plaga, múrlocs salvajes y la sombra invasora de los no-muertos. En la época dorada de la Alianza de Lordaeron, el Lago Lordamere se encontraba en la encrucijada del poder humano. La Capital de Lordaeron custodiaba sus costas septentrionales, la ciudad-estado hechicera de Dalaran se alzaba cerca de su límite meridional y el reino de Alterac bordeaba su escarpado extremo oriental. Barcos mercantes y embarcaciones pesqueras surcaban antaño sin temor su amplia y neblinosa extensión. Tras la devastación de la Tercera Guerra, el lago pasó de ser un centro neurálgico del comercio a una barrera natural que separaba las tierras de Tirisfal y Argénteos, en manos de los Renegados, de las traicioneras alturas de Alterac.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Human"]="The quiet, foggy waters of Lordamere are a somber reminder of the ruined glory of the northern human kingdoms, which once traded freely across its shores.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Lordamere Lake serves as both a defensive moat protecting Tirisfal and an active frontline where Scourge remnants on Fenris Isle must be purged."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lordamere Lake was bordered by three major human kingdoms during the height of the Alliance of Lordaeron: the Kingdom of Lordaeron to the north and west, Dalaran to the south, and Alterac along its eastern mountain bluffs.",["al"]={"who lived on lordamere lake","lordamere lake history","kingdoms around lordamere"},["q"]="What kingdoms historically bordered Lordamere Lake?"},{["a"]="Fenris Isle is currently held by agents of the Scourge under the command of the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, though they face relentless assaults from the Forsaken and constant pressure from ravenous worgen.",["al"]={"who is on fenris isle","fenris island lordamere","fenris isle ruler"},["q"]="Who controls Fenris Isle in the middle of the lake?"},{["a"]="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of small islands situated in the eastern portion of Lordamere Lake, east of Fenris Isle. They have been overrun and claimed by hostile Vile Fin murlocs.",["al"]={"dawning isles location","islands in lordamere lake","dawning isles monsters"},["q"]="What are the Dawning Isles?"},{["a"]="The lake was named in conjunction with the nearby Capital City and kingdom of Lordaeron, which took their name from the ancient human general Lordain.",["al"]={"lordamere name origin","why is it called lordamere"},["q"]="How did the lake get its name?"}},["kw"]={"alterac mountains","dawning isles","fenris isle","lake lordamere","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},["n"]="Lordamere Lake",["s"]="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, bordered by Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains. Once the bustling aquatic heart of human civilization in the north, its cold waters and islands are now haunted by Scourge necromancers, feral murlocs, and the spreading shadow of the undead.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In the golden age of the Alliance of Lordaeron, Lordamere Lake sat at the crossroads of human power. The Capital City of Lordaeron guarded its northern shores, the sorcerous city-state of Dalaran rose near its southern reach, and the kingdom of Alterac lined its mountainous eastern edge. Merchant vessels and fishing boats once crossed its broad, mist-covered expanse without fear. Following the devastation of the Third War, the lake was transformed from a hub of commerce into a natural barrier dividing the Forsaken-held lands of Tirisfal and Silverpine from the treacherous heights of Alterac.",["t"]="Heart of the Fallen Kingdoms"},{["b"]="Today, navigating the dark waters of Lordamere is fraught with peril. At the center of the lake sits Fenris Isle, where Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw and his undead thralls hold out against the Forsaken, while vicious worgen prowl the vicinity. Further east lie the Dawning Isles, completely overrun by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs. From the ruins around Dalaran to the shoreline of the Undercity, the lake is no longer a peaceful highway, but a drowned frontier contested by remnant monsters and the armies of the dead.",["t"]="A Contested Expanse"}}}}}
t["subzone:lushwater-oasis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,364,22.501.0,53.138.0,29.174.0,30.153.0,39.206.0",["h"]="1b8712",["n"]="Oasis Aguaverde",["s"]="Oasis Aguaverde. El Oasis Aguaverde es uno de los tres abrevaderos rebosantes de vida ubicados en los áridos Baldíos, situado justo al sur de El Cruce. A pesar de su apariencia exuberante, el oasis entraña un gran peligro: está infestado de agresivos centauros Kolkar y alberga la entrada a las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Sus aguas contaminadas son bien conocidas por los pescadores que buscan el peculiar Pez descarriado. Situado a una corta marcha al sur de El Cruce, el Oasis Aguaverde ofrece un respiro engañoso en medio de la extensión calcinada por el sol de Los Baldíos. Aunque sus copas de palmeras y sus manantiales de agua dulce atraen a bestias sedientas de toda la sabana, los centauros Kolkar reclaman sus orillas, al acecho para masacrar tanto a las presas como a los viajeros incautos. El oasis es también la puerta de entrada a las Cuevas de los Lamentos, cuyas extensas redes subterráneas filtran energías corruptoras en las pozas superiores, engendrando una fauna antinatural y extrañas mutaciones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Lushwater Oasis exhibits a troubling, unnatural overgrowth driven by the twisted energies escaping the nearby Wailing Caverns.",["profession:Cooking"]="The pools here are among the few waters where anglers can land Deviate Fish, a vital ingredient prized across Kalimdor for preparing Savory Deviate Delights."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance to the Wailing Caverns cavern system lies carved into the natural rock faces overlooking the eastern side of Lushwater Oasis.",["al"]={"where is wc","wc cave entrance","wailing caverns entrance"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Wailing Caverns located?"},{["a"]="The Kolkar centaur maintain a dominant presence throughout the oasis, using the lush cover to hunt passing wildlife and attack travelers making their way from the Crossroads.",["al"]={"who lives at lushwater oasis","lushwater enemies","centaur at the oasis"},["q"]="Who controls Lushwater Oasis?"},{["a"]="The deep energies leaking from the Wailing Caverns have corrupted the waterways across the oasis, causing local fish to mutate into unusual Deviate Fish.",["al"]={"deviate fish location","why deviate fish","mutated fish oasis"},["q"]="Why are the fish here strange?"},{["a"]="During the orcs' Long March through the Barrens alongside the tauren, Thrall led his troops through the region's scattered oases to secure vital drinking water while fending off relentless centaur ambushes.",["al"]={"thrall long march oasis","orcs in barrens oasis"},["q"]="Did Thrall's Horde travel through here?"}},["kw"]={"crossroads","deviate fish","kolkar","lushwater oasis","the barrens","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lushwater Oasis",["s"]="Lushwater Oasis is one of the three life-giving watering holes nestled in the arid Barrens, located just south of the Crossroads. Despite its verdant appearance, the oasis is fraught with danger, infested by aggressive Kolkar centaur and harboring the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. Its tainted waters are well-known to anglers seeking the peculiar Deviate Fish.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated a short march south of the Crossroads, Lushwater Oasis offers a deceptive respite amid the sun-bleached expanse of the Barrens. While its palm canopies and fresh springs draw thirsty beasts from across the savanna, Kolkar centaur claim the banks, lying in wait to butcher both game and unwary travelers. The oasis is also the gateway to the Wailing Caverns, whose sprawling underground networks seep corruptive energies into the pools above, breeding unnatural wildlife and bizarre mutations.",["t"]="A Precarious Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:maclure-vineyards"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,281,16.441.0,19.440.1,46.246.0,23.216.0,35.187.0,34.148.0",["h"]="031d51",["n"]="Los Viñedos de Maclure",["s"]="Los Viñedos de Maclure. Los Viñedos de Maclure son una extensa finca agrícola situada en el sur del Bosque de Elwynn, propiedad de la familia Maclure. Aunque es conocida por producir uvas y vino para el reino de Ventormenta, la granja es igualmente famosa por una amarga y continua disputa con sus vecinos, la familia Stonefield. Enclavados en las exuberantes colinas del sur del Bosque de Elwynn, Los Viñedos de Maclure deberían ser un remanso de paz dedicado a la viticultura y la agricultura. En su lugar, el trabajo diario se ve ensombrecido por una encarnizada y prolongada rivalidad con los Stonefield, situados al final del camino. Las acusaciones de robo y el rencor están muy arraigados entre ambas familias, lo que mantiene los ánimos encendidos incluso cuando problemas comunes, como jabalíes hambrientos al acecho y kóbolds invasores, amenazan ambos hogares.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The estate serves as an important breadbasket and vineyard supplying the nearby settlements of Goldshire and Stormwind City with food and spirits.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, the vineyard feud is a classic example of countryside stubbornness, reminding travelers that even within the heartland, neighbors often bicker over fences while larger perils loom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The rivalry is a long-standing rural feud built on years of mistrust, petty accusations, and stubborn pride. Neither family trusts the other an inch, blaming each other for lost goods and livestock, though neither has outright proof of foul play.",["al"]={"maclure stonefield feud","why do they hate each other","family feud"},["q"]="Why are the Maclures and Stonefields fighting?"},{["a"]="Maybell is the daughter of the Maclure household. She has secretly fallen in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield, defying her family's bitter hatred of their neighbors in the hope of finding a way for them to be together.",["al"]={"maybell","maclure daughter"},["q"]="Who is Maybell Maclure?"},{["a"]="Aside from family disputes, the vineyards are plagued by ravenous wild boars trampling the crops and vines, as well as wandering kobolds raiding nearby fields from surrounding gold mines.",["al"]={"vineyard dangers","boars at maclure"},["q"]="What threats do the vineyards face?"},{["a"]="The Maclure family cultivates grapevines to supply wine and fresh fruit to tavern-keepers and merchants throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City.",["al"]={"what grows here","maclure crops"},["q"]="What do the Maclures produce here?"}},["kw"]={"boars","elwynn","gerard","maclure","maybell","stonefield","vineyard","wine"},["n"]="Maclure Vineyards",["s"]="Maclure Vineyards is a sprawling agricultural estate in southern Elwynn Forest owned by the Maclure family. While known for producing grapes and wine for the kingdom of Stormwind, the farmstead is equally infamous for an ongoing, bitter feud with the neighboring Stonefield family.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled in the lush hills of southern Elwynn Forest, the Maclure Vineyards should be a peaceful haven of winecraft and farming. Instead, everyday labor is overshadowed by a vicious, long-standing rivalry with the Stonefields just down the road. Accusations of theft and bad blood run deep between the households, keeping tempers flaring even as common troubles—like hungry prowling boars and encroaching kobolds—threaten both homesteads.",["t"]="A Bitter Harvest"},{["b"]="Despite the fierce animosity between the two patriarchs, young love has crossed the boundary lines. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield have fallen secretly in love, meeting in hidden groves away from their parents' suspicious eyes. Those passing through the vineyards often find themselves drawn into running secret messages, resolving petty grievances, and trying to help the young couple escape the shadow of their families' grudge.",["t"]="A Forbidden Romance"}}}}}
t["subzone:mage-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,378,21.510.0,27.491.1,29.257.0,45.246.0,43.254.0,34.193.0",["h"]="6e7855",["n"]="Barrio de los Magos",["s"]="Barrio de los Magos. El Barrio de los Magos conforma el corazón arcano de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, situado al otro lado de los canales, en la esquina suroeste de la capital. Elevándose sobre sus calles empedradas y sus esotéricas tiendas especializadas se alza el Sagrario del Mago, donde los evocadores del reino perfeccionan su arte. Bajo la superficie erudita del distrito también yacen sombríos rincones que albergan a practicantes de artes mucho más oscuras. Accesible mediante puentes que cruzan los canales desde la Plaza de la Catedral o el Distrito de Mercaderes, el Barrio de los Magos atiende por completo las necesidades místicas de la Alianza. En torno a la aguja del Sagrario del Mago, lanzadores de conjuros humanos y aliados se reúnen para estudiar el tejido de la magia arcana e instruir a aprendices. Las calles circundantes están repletas de proveedores de telas para sastrería, componentes, suministros alquímicos y bastones encantados, creando un distrito insular dedicado a la investigación y a la defensa del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The district serves as your central home in Stormwind, offering master trainers and spell reagents inside the Wizard's Sanctum.",["class:Warlock"]="Beneath the public guise of The Slaughtered Lamb tavern lies the hidden coven where practitioners of the dark arts convene to train and summon minions in secret."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Wizard's Sanctum is the prominent tower dominating the Mage Quarter. It serves as the primary academy, library, and training grounds for Stormwind's mages, housing scholars, mystic trainers, and defensive spellcasters tasked with protecting the capital.",["al"]={"mage tower","wizards sanctum","mage sanctum stormwind"},["q"]="What is the Wizard's Sanctum?"},{["a"]="Warlocks gather secretly beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, an unassuming tavern in the quarter. Down in its crypts and hidden cellars, practitioners of fel magic can study dark rituals, summon demons, and train outside the scrutiny of the city guard.",["al"]={"warlock trainer location","slaughtered lamb basement","stormwind warlock trainers"},["q"]="Where can warlocks train in the Mage Quarter?"},{["a"]="The district is filled with specialty trades catering to casters and crafters. Visitors can find tailoring shops like Duncan's Textiles and Larson Clothiers, alchemy and herbalism merchants, enchanting vendors, pyrotechnic suppliers, and staff merchants.",["al"]={"mage quarter vendors","what shops are here","stores in mage quarter"},["q"]="What kind of shops are in the Mage Quarter?"},{["a"]="The Mage Quarter occupies the southwestern corner of Stormwind City. It can be accessed directly by crossing the bridges that span the Canals from either the Trade District or Cathedral Square.",["al"]={"where is mage quarter","how to get to mage quarter","directions to mage quarter"},["q"]="How do you reach the Mage Quarter?"}},["kw"]={"arcane","blue recluse","canals","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","wizard's sanctum"},["n"]="Mage Quarter",["s"]="The Mage Quarter forms the arcane heart of Stormwind City, resting across the canals in the capital's southwestern corner. Towering over its cobblestone streets and esoteric specialty shops stands the Wizard's Sanctum, where the kingdom's conjurers hone their craft. Beneath the district's scholarly surface also lie shadowy recesses, harboring practitioners of far darker arts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Reachable by bridges crossing the canals from Cathedral Square or the Trade District, the Mage Quarter caters entirely to the mystical needs of the Alliance. Centered around the spire of the Wizard's Sanctum, human and allied spellcasters gather to study the weave of arcane magic and train apprentices. The surrounding streets are crowded with purveyors of tailoring cloth, reagents, alchemical supplies, and enchanted staves, creating an insular district dedicated to research and the defense of the kingdom.",["t"]="Sanctum of the Arcane"},{["b"]="Not all sorcery practiced in the quarter is approved by the kingdom's high conjurers. While establishments like The Blue Recluse offer quiet refuge for scholars, the infamous Slaughtered Lamb tavern conceals a covert coven of warlocks in its subterranean crypts. There, out of sight of the city guard and the holy eyes of Cathedral Square, demonologists study forbidden fel rites and bind otherworldly entities while masquerading beneath the district's general tolerance of mystic anomalies.",["t"]="Secrets Beneath the Surface"}}}}}
t["subzone:magic-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,245,23.561.0,32.481.0,41.233.0,53.301.0,40.165.0,35.117.0",["h"]="d5322b",["n"]="Barrio de la Magia",["s"]="Barrio de la Magia. El Barrio de la Magia es el distrito noreste de Entrañas, y sirve como centro para el estudio arcano y la hechicería oscura de los Renegados. Dominado por un ominoso Templo de los Condenados, el barrio alberga a practicantes tanto de las artes arcanas como de las viles. Ocupando el cuadrante noreste de la ciudad subterránea, el Barrio de la Magia es el lugar donde los Renegados preservan su legado arcano y profundizan en metodologías más oscuras. La pieza central del distrito es un imponente Templo de los Condenados, una reliquia arquitectónica de diseño de la Plaga que ha sido reutilizada por los no-muertos de libre albedrío. Bajo sus techos abovedados y sombríos, los magos practican sutiles manipulaciones de energías mágicas junto a brujos que comulgan con entidades demoníacas, convirtiendo al barrio en el nexo de poder intelectual e investigación oculta de Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The Magic Quarter is the heart of Forsaken wizardry, offering training in arcane arts and teleportation networks that link the Undercity with the wider Horde.",["class:Warlock"]="Within the dark alcoves of the Temple of the Damned, warlocks summon demonic minions and hone shadow magic far from the judgmental eyes of the Alliance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Magic Quarter serves as the center of arcane and demonic studies for the Forsaken. It houses class trainers for mages and warlocks, portal masters connecting to other cities, and tailoring professionals who weave enchanted cloth.",["al"]={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter purpose","undercity magic district"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Magic Quarter?"},{["a"]="When the Undercity was carved out beneath the ruins of Capital City by the Scourge, they erected structures like the Temple of the Damned. When Sylvanas and her free-willed Forsaken seized the subterranean complex, they claimed these existing facilities and repurposed them for their own spellcasters.",["al"]={"temple of the damned undercity","why temple of the damned here","scourge building undercity"},["q"]="Why is there a Temple of the Damned in the Undercity?"},{["a"]="Mages, warlocks, and demon trainers instruct practitioners within the quarter, while portal specialists and tailoring artisans offer training in transport and craft.",["al"]={"trainers in magic quarter","who trains here","magic quarter classes"},["q"]="Who can be trained in the Magic Quarter?"},{["a"]="It is situated in the northeastern quadrant of the Undercity, directly across the central ring from the Apothecarium.",["al"]={"where is magic quarter","magic quarter location","find magic quarter"},["q"]="Where is the Magic Quarter located?"}},["kw"]={"forsaken","mage","magic quarter","portal trainer","tailoring","temple of the damned","undercity","warlock"},["n"]="Magic Quarter",["s"]="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the center for Forsaken arcane study and dark spellcraft. Dominated by an ominous Temple of the Damned, the quarter houses practitioners of both the arcane and fel arts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying the northeastern quadrant of the subterranean city, the Magic Quarter is where the Forsaken preserve their arcane heritage and delve into darker methodologies. The centerpiece of the district is a looming Temple of the Damned, an architectural relic of Scourge design that has been repurposed by the free-willed undead. Beneath its vaulted, shadowy ceilings, mages practice subtle manipulations of magical energies alongside warlocks communing with demonic entities, making the quarter the nexus of intellectual power and occult research in Lordaeron.",["t"]="A Conclave of Dark Arts"},{["b"]="Beyond the study of raw evocation and summoning, the Magic Quarter functions as an essential civic hub for spellcasters. Portal trainers maintain transport links across Horde territories, while master tailors work with magically infused fabrics to craft robes and shrouds. Unlike Dalaran's strict segregation between academic wizardry and forbidden magic, the Forsaken blend arcane curiosity and fel power openly within these halls to secure their place against their many enemies.",["t"]="Scholars, Weavers, and Summoners"}}}}}
t["subzone:main-hall-northshire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,334,18.494.0,37.202.0,30.208.0",["h"]="352c28",["n"]="Sala Principal (Villanorte)",["s"]="Sala Principal (Villanorte). La Sala Principal es la sala central de entrada de la Abadía de Villanorte en el Bosque de Elwynn. Sirve como la encrucijada principal que conecta los terrenos de la abadía con su torre superior, la Sala de Armas y el Ala de la Biblioteca. Aquí, los aventureros humanos recién reclutados se presentan para recibir sus asignaciones iniciales al servicio del Reino de Ventormenta. Cruzar los grandes arcos de la Abadía de Villanorte lleva a los visitantes directamente a la sala principal. Como núcleo central del edificio, canaliza a los aprendices y al personal clerical que llegan entre las distintas alas de la abadía: la marcial Sala de Armas a un lado, el ala de la biblioteca, dedicada al estudio, al otro y las escaleras que suben a la torre de la abadía. El tranquilo santuario de la sala se ve atenuado por el continuo conflicto en el valle, mientras los oficiales reúnen a los recién llegados capacitados para defender las fronteras del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey marks the beginning of their journey in service of Stormwind and the Holy Light."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Main Hall serves as the central reception chamber and crossroads of Northshire Abbey. It directs recruits, priests, and visitors into the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and the abbey's upper tower.",["al"]={"what is main hall","northshire main hall use"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Main Hall?"},{["a"]="Officers and clerics of the Stormwind defense stationed in the Main Hall evaluate incoming adventurers, providing them with their first marching orders to clear out threats encroaching on the abbey's grounds.",["al"]={"who gives quests here","abbey commander"},["q"]="Who directs new recruits here?"}},["kw"]={"abbey","elwynn","hall of arms","library wing","main hall","northshire","stormwind"},["n"]="Main Hall (Northshire)",["s"]="The Main Hall is the central entrance chamber of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary crossroads connecting the abbey's grounds to its upper tower, the Hall of Arms, and the Library Wing. Here, newly recruited human adventurers report to receive their initial assignments in service of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stepping through the grand archways of Northshire Abbey brings visitors directly into the Main Hall. As the building's central hub, it channels arriving trainees and clerical staff between the abbey's distinct wings: the martial Hall of Arms on one side, the scholastic Library Wing on the other, and the stairs rising into the abbey tower. The quiet sanctuary of the hall is tempered by the ongoing strife in the valley, as officers rally able-bodied newcomers to defend the kingdom's borders.",["t"]="Heart of the Abbey"}}}}}
t["subzone:malaka-jin"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,305,17.479.0,25.373.0,19.227.0,24.169.0,27.211.0,30.203.0",["h"]="a7d729",["n"]="Malaka'jin",["s"]="Malaka'jin. Malaka'jin es un pequeño campamento de la Horda enclavado en las colinas bajas de Sierra Espolón, justo al sur de Poblado Tótem Siniestro. Habitado principalmente por cazadores trols de Lanza Negra, el asentamiento sirve como una rústica parada y puesto de caza para los viajeros que ascienden hacia los escarpados picos desde Los Baldíos. Escondido cerca del camino principal hacia Sierra Espolón, Malaka'jin ofrece un grato santuario para los caminantes de la Horda que se aventuran en las disputadas alturas. La aldea alberga a un grupo de curtidos cazadores trols que se ganan la vida entre los riscos y matorrales. A pesar de su vida modesta, estos cazadores ofrecen suministros, comercian con sus presas recién cazadas con los aventureros fatigados y vigilan con cautela a la hostil fauna montañosa y a los beligerantes tauren Tótem Siniestro que acechan más arriba por los senderos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Malaka'jin serves as the Horde's southernmost threshold in Stonetalon, offering a vital waystation on the trail between the Barrens and the northern mountain strongholds.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Malaka'jin is a proud demonstration of troll self-reliance and tracking prowess, carving out a home in the rugged heights far from Kalimdor's tropical shores."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Malaka'jin is a small Horde village and outpost in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. It is inhabited by a community of Darkspear troll hunters who provide shelter, trade, and supplies to travelers climbing up from the Barrens.",["al"]={"where is malakajin","what is this place","malakajin stonetalon"},["q"]="What is Malaka'jin?"},{["a"]="The settlement is populated almost entirely by troll hunters. They sustain themselves by hunting the mountain game and trading meat and leather with passing adventurers.",["al"]={"malakajin npcs","who is here","trolls in stonetalon"},["q"]="Who lives in Malaka'jin?"},{["a"]="Aside from fierce mountain predators, the village is situated directly south of the hostile Grimtotem Post, leaving the small troll camp constantly vigilant against aggression from the antagonistic tauren tribe.",["al"]={"malakajin enemies","who attacks malakajin"},["q"]="What threats face the camp?"},{["a"]="No. In this era, Malaka'jin has no flight master. Adventurers traveling through the Stonetalon Mountains must rely on the flight master at Sun Rock Retreat further northwest or traverse the road on foot.",["al"]={"malakajin flight path","fly to malakajin"},["q"]="Is there a flight master here?"}},["kw"]={"darkspear","grimtotem","horde","hunters","malaka'jin","outpost","stonetalon","trolls"},["n"]="Malaka'jin",["s"]="Malaka'jin is a small Horde encampment nestled in the lower hills of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the Grimtotem Post. Inhabited primarily by Darkspear troll hunters, the settlement serves as a rustic waystation and hunting outpost for travelers ascending into the rugged peaks from the Barrens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away near the main path into the Stonetalon Mountains, Malaka'jin provides a welcome sanctuary for Horde wanderers venturing into contested heights. The village is home to a band of rugged troll hunters who eke out a living off the crags and scrublands. While living modestly, these hunters offer supplies, trade their fresh game to weary adventurers, and keep a wary eye on the hostile mountain wildlife and the belligerent Grimtotem tauren lurking further up the trails.",["t"]="A Hunters' Refuge"},{["b"]="Perched precariously near the boundary of the Barrens, Malaka'jin marks one of the earliest Horde presences established in Stonetalon. Though small and quiet compared to the major fortress at Sun Rock Retreat further north, it functions as a vital logistical anchor, allowing Horde trackers to monitor tribal unrest and secure the winding roads against encroaching threats.",["t"]="A Foothold in the Heights"}}}}}
t["subzone:malden-s-orchard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,362,18.448.0,22.486.1,15.174.0,33.159.0,34.186.0,48.140.0",["h"]="68cc41",["n"]="Huerta de Malden",["s"]="Huerta de Malden. La Huerta de Malden es una granja en ruinas situada en el norte del Bosque de Argénteos, llamada así por el propietario humano que huyó durante la invasión de la Plaga en Lordaeron. Abandonada desde hace mucho tiempo, sus oscuros árboles de hoja perenne crecen descontrolados mientras feroces huargos negros acechan los terrenos. La derruida cabaña de la huerta sirvió de refugio temporal para un explorador Renegado que quedó aislado de su unidad. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, esta hacienda suministraba fruta fresca a las ciudades de Lordaeron, cuidada por un granjero llamado Malden. Cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino, Malden abandonó sus tierras para huir de la peste. En los años transcurridos desde entonces, la huerta ha quedado asfixiada bajo las densas y oscuras nieblas del Bosque de Argénteos. Los árboles de hoja perenne permanecen sin podar y sus frutos se pudren sin recoger en ramas marchitas, dejando el terreno completamente dominado por depredadores salvajes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Travelers moving south from the Sepulcher or the Tirisfal border must tread carefully around the orchard due to the aggressive worg packs nesting on the farm.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the orchard is a reminder of human ruin and a contested piece of northern Silverpine that Deathstalker scouts must secure against feral beasts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Malden was a human farmer who lived here before the fall of Lordaeron. He abandoned the orchard and fled for his life when the Scourge invaded the realm during the Third War.",["al"]={"malden lore","who owned the orchard","who is malden"},["q"]="Who was Malden?"},{["a"]="With no living tenders to defend the farmstead, wild black worgs prowling Silverpine Forest claimed the dense grove and abandoned yard as their pack territory.",["al"]={"why are there worgs here","malden orchard dogs","worg infestation"},["q"]="Why is the orchard full of worgs?"},{["a"]="Deathstalker Erland McKree was trapped inside the cottage. Sent on a reconnaissance mission by the Forsaken, he was ambushed by the orchard's worgs and holed up inside until aid arrived.",["al"]={"cottage scout","who is in the house","deathstalker in the cabin"},["q"]="Who is trapped inside the cottage?"},{["a"]="No. The dark trees have not been tended in years, and their fruit rots on the branches amidst the decay spreading through Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"is the fruit edible","malden's orchard harvest","can you pick fruit"},["q"]="Does anyone harvest fruit from this orchard now?"}},["kw"]={"cottage","erland mckree","ivar patch","malden","malden's orchard","maldens orchard","silverpine","worgs"},["n"]="Malden's Orchard",["s"]="Malden's Orchard is a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest, named after the human owner who fled during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Long abandoned, its dark evergreen trees sit overgrown while vicious black worgs stalk the grounds. The orchard's crumbling cottage served as a temporary refuge for a stranded Forsaken scout cut off from his unit.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this homestead supplied fresh fruit to the towns of Lordaeron, tended by a farmer named Malden. When the Scourge tore through the kingdom, Malden abandoned his land to flee the plague. In the years since, the orchard has choked under the dark, encroaching mists of Silverpine Forest. The evergreen trees remain unpruned and their fruit rots ungathered on blighted boughs, leaving the plot entirely reclaimed by wild predators.",["t"]="A Blighted Harvest"},{["b"]="The overgrown orchard has become a hunting ground for territorial black worgs, making it a hazardous route through northern Silverpine. During a reconnaissance mission for the Deathstalkers, the scout Erland McKree was dispatched to survey the area but found himself overwhelmed by the beasts. Pinned inside Malden's dilapidated cottage for days, Erland survived only until Forsaken reinforcements could break through the pack and escort him back to his fellow scouts at the Ivar Patch.",["t"]="Trapped in the Cottage"}}}}}
t["subzone:menethil-harbor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,461,22.571.0,28.516.0,46.228.0,26.258.0,31.231.0,44.285.0",["h"]="f0c83a",["n"]="Puerto de Menethil",["s"]="Puerto de Menethil. El Puerto de Menethil es una ciudad portuaria enana fuertemente fortificada, situada en una isla frente a la costa occidental de Los Humedales. Construida sobre un antiguo astillero orco y bautizada en honor al rey Terenas Menethil II, sirve como la principal arteria marítima que conecta los Reinos del Este con las distantes costas de Kalimdor. Al abrigo de enormes almenas de piedra y de las robustas torres del Castillo de Menethil, es un bullicioso punto de encuentro para mercaderes, soldados de permiso y curtidos aventureros. El emplazamiento del Puerto de Menethil sirvió por primera vez al Jefe de Guerra Orgrim Martillo Maldito durante la Segunda Guerra, cuando la Horda construyó una armada de invasión con madera y hierro saqueados de Khaz Modan. Tras la derrota de los orcos, el Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente supervisó la reconstrucción del fondeadero para convertirlo en un refugio de primer orden para la Alianza, dándole nombre como tributo al difunto rey Terenas Menethil II de Lordaeron. A pesar de su remota ubicación pantanosa, sigue siendo un bastión fuertemente defendido, reforzado por murallas colosales, una única calzada con puente y las cuatro torres de vigilancia de piedra del Castillo de Menethil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For any Alliance traveler journeying west, Menethil Harbor is the vital staging ground and sole maritime bridge linking the Eastern Kingdoms to Theramore and Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though bearing a human king's name, this port is maintained primarily by dwarven stonework and manned by Ironforge guards holding the outer threshold of Khaz Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Vessels departing the docks of Menethil Harbor cross the Great Sea to the continent of Kalimdor. Scheduled passenger ships run regular routes to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and north to the night elven haven of Auberdine.",["al"]={"menethil harbor boat","where does the boat go","menethil ferries","kalimdor boats"},["q"]="Where do the ships in Menethil Harbor sail to?"},{["a"]="Menethil Harbor operates as an Alliance settlement under the authority of Ironforge. Captain Stoutfist commands the town guard and coordinates harbor defense out of Menethil Keep, keeping the docks secure from swamp beasts, renegade orcs, and inland raiders.",["al"]={"who is in charge of menethil","menethil harbor leader","who leads menethil"},["q"]="Who rules Menethil Harbor?"},{["a"]="The harbor was named by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore after the Second War in tribute to King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, whose leadership united the human, dwarven, and elven realms into the original Alliance of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why menethil harbor","menethil name origin","who is menethil"},["q"]="Why is the town named Menethil?"},{["a"]="The harbor faces persistent danger from the Dragonmaw clan lurking in the Wetlands hills, who regularly try to cut off the pass through Dun Algaz to starve the port of reinforcements. Dark Iron incursions to the north near Dun Modr and marauding raptors add to the garrison's troubles.",["al"]={"is menethil harbor in danger","menethil threats","wetlands orcs menethil"},["q"]="What threats does the harbor face right now?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","boat","deepwater","docks","ferry","harbor","menethil","stoutfist","theramore","wetlands"},["n"]="Menethil Harbor",["s"]="Menethil Harbor is a heavily fortified dwarven port town perched on an island off the western shore of the Wetlands. Built over an old Orcish shipyard and named after King Terenas Menethil II, it acts as the primary maritime lifeline connecting the Eastern Kingdoms to the distant shores of Kalimdor. Sheltered behind massive stone battlements and the sturdy towers of Menethil Keep, it is a bustling hub for merchants, off-duty soldiers, and salty adventurers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The site of Menethil Harbor first served Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer during the Second War, when the Horde constructed an invasion armada out of timber and iron ransacked from Khaz Modan. After the orcs were routed, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore oversaw the rebuilding of the anchorage into a premier Alliance haven, naming it in tribute to the late King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron. Despite its remote marshland setting, it remains a heavily defended bastion, reinforced by massive walls, a single bridged causeway, and the four stone watchtowers of Menethil Keep.",["t"]="A Port Carved from War"},{["b"]="Today, the harbor is the grand crossroads of the Alliance. Ships steam continually across the ocean toward Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and Auberdine in darkshore, carrying trade, diplomats, and off-duty Kul Tiran marines blowing their wages at the Deepwater Tavern. Yet peace is fragile here: inland supply paths through Dun Algaz are regularly contested by the Dragonmaw clan, while hostile Dark Iron raiders pressure the northern marshes, leaving Captain Stoutfist and the harbor garrison on constant alert.",["t"]="Gateway Across the Great Sea"}}}}}
t["subzone:merchant-coast"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,248,35.506.0,36.200.0,49.201.0,37.222.0",["h"]="3c2c2e",["n"]="La Costa Mercante",["s"]="La Costa Mercante. La Costa Mercante es el tramo del litoral oriental de Los Baldíos que bordea el Mare Magnum. Dominada por el bullicioso puerto goblin de Trinquete, la costa debe su nombre al lucrativo comercio marítimo, aunque los piratas se la disputan constantemente. A lo largo del borde oriental de Los Baldíos, La Costa Mercante sirve como una arteria marítima vital que conecta el centro de Kalimdor con los Reinos del Este y Theramore. Su nombre rinde homenaje a los laboriosos comerciantes goblins del Cártel Bonvapor, cuyo puerto neutral de Trinquete gestiona cargamentos para cualquiera que disponga de monedas. Sin embargo, las rutas marítimas abiertas atraen a algo más que navíos mercantes: los filibusteros del Mar del Sur merodean por las arenas y las aguas cercanas, acechando a los barcos mercantes y estableciendo operaciones ilícitas a lo largo de las playas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance maintains a nearby naval presence at Northwatch Hold, keeping a wary eye on both the goblin trade passing through Ratchet and the unruly Southsea pirates along the shore.",["faction:Horde"]="The Merchant Coast is the Horde's primary commercial lifeline to the sea in the Barrens, making the security of Ratchet and suppression of local pirates vital for regional supply lines."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shoreline earned its name from the lucrative trade conducted through the goblin port of Ratchet. Steamwheedle merchants move cargo across the Great Sea from this coast to ports all around Azeroth.",["al"]={"merchant coast name origin","why called merchant coast"},["q"]="Why is it called the Merchant Coast?"},{["a"]="The most prominent settlement is Ratchet, a neutral goblin port city run by Gazlowe. Farther south along the coast lies the Alliance stronghold of Northwatch Hold, while Fray Island sits just offshore.",["al"]={"towns on merchant coast","what is on merchant coast"},["q"]="What major settlements are on the Merchant Coast?"},{["a"]="While Ratchet controls the immediate harbor, the Southsea Freebooters have established encampments along the surrounding beaches. These pirates actively disrupt trade, rob goblin convoys, and challenge Ratchet's authority.",["al"]={"pirates on merchant coast","who is attacking merchant coast"},["q"]="Who controls the beaches around here?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","great sea","merchant coast","ratchet","southsea freebooters","steamwheedle cartel"},["n"]="Merchant Coast",["s"]="The Merchant Coast is the stretch of eastern shoreline in the Barrens bordering the Great Sea. Dominated by the bustling goblin port of Ratchet, the coast derives its name from lucrative sea trade, though it remains constantly contested by pirates.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running along the eastern edge of the Barrens, the Merchant Coast serves as a vital maritime artery connecting central Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms and Theramore. Its name honors the industrious goblin traders of the Steamwheedle Cartel, whose neutral port of Ratchet handles cargo for anyone with coin. However, the open sea lanes attract more than merchant vessels: Southsea Freebooters prowl the sands and nearby waters, preying on merchant ships and setting up illicit operations along the beaches.",["t"]="A Gateway for Commerce and Conflict"}}}}}
t["subzone:military-ward"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,282,26.548.0,31.342.0,26.158.0,42.150.0,37.166.0,41.179.0",["h"]="235709",["n"]="Sala Militar",["s"]="Sala Militar. La Sala Militar sirve como el corazón marcial de Forjaz, albergando la infraestructura de mando de la ciudad, maestros de armas y barracones. Marcado por llamativos estandartes rojos, es el lugar donde los soldados, cazadores e ingenieros de asedio enanos entrenan junto a máquinas de asedio mecanizadas y máquinas voladoras. Situada en el perímetro norte de la fortaleza de la montaña, la Sala Militar concentra las fuerzas defensivas de Forjaz en una bulliciosa zona de concentración. El complejo central, la Sala de Armas, acoge a instructores de guerreros y cazadores, maestros de batalla y hangares que albergan máquinas voladoras y tanques de vapor enanos. Alrededor de las plazas de instrucción y los muñecos de entrenamiento se encuentran puntos de suministros como Armaduras de Placas y Malla de Craghelm, Suministros de Caza de Goldfury y Armería Timberline, lo que convierte al distrito en el principal punto de preparación para los montañeros y defensores de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Rangers and mountaineers will find beast masters and supplies in the Hall of Arms, alongside Goldfury's Hunting Supplies for munitions and gear.",["class:Warrior"]="The Military Ward is the chief martial hub in Ironforge, offering warrior trainers, training dummies for combat practice, and weapon masters to broaden your battlefield arsenal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the martial quarter of Ironforge, serving as the central base for the dwarven army, warrior and hunter trainers, weapons merchants, and siege machinery.",["al"]={"military ward ironforge","ironforge barracks","ironforge warrior district"},["q"]="What is the Military Ward?"},{["a"]="Weapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand is stationed at Timberline Arms within the Military Ward, offering training in various armaments to Alliance fighters.",["al"]={"ironforge weapon master","where is buliwyf stonehand","learn weapons ironforge"},["q"]="Where can I train in weapons in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The Hall of Arms functions as the military headquarters, containing combat instructors, battlemasters, and large bays storing steam tanks and dwarven flying machines.",["al"]={"hall of arms ironforge","what is in hall of arms","ironforge siege engines"},["q"]="What is kept inside the Hall of Arms?"},{["a"]="Ironforge's districts use specific heraldic colors for navigation and tradition; the Military Ward is draped in bold red banners to represent the martial arm of the mountain city.",["al"]={"military ward colors","red banners ironforge"},["q"]="Why are the banners red in this district?"}},["kw"]={"buliwyf stonehand","flying machines","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","steam tanks","timberline arms"},["n"]="Military Ward",["s"]="The Military Ward serves as the martial heart of Ironforge, housing the city's command infrastructure, weapons masters, and barracks. Marked by bold red banners, it is where dwarven soldiers, hunters, and siege engineers train alongside mechanized siege engines and flying machines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within the northern perimeter of the mountain fortress, the Military Ward concentrates Ironforge's defensive forces into a bustling staging ground. The central complex, the Hall of Arms, accommodates warrior and hunter trainers, battlemasters, and hangars housing dwarven flying machines and steam tanks. Surrounding the drill squares and training dummies are supply outlets such as Craghelm's Plate and Chain, Goldfury's Hunting Supplies, and Timberline Arms, making the ward the primary staging point for mountaineers and city defenders.",["t"]="The Anvil of Dwarven Might"},{["b"]="Distinguished from the pale blue of the Commons and the fiery orange of the Great Forge, the Military Ward is draped in martial red banners. Between drills and weapons inspections, soldiers and off-duty guards gather at Bruuk's Corner for an ale, while Weapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand instructs recruits in ancient dwarven martial traditions.",["t"]="A Garrison under Banners of War"}}}}}
t["subzone:mirror-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,296,15.590.0,29.236.0,35.262.0,50.177.0",["h"]="0fa422",["n"]="Lago Espejo",["s"]="Lago Espejo. El Lago Espejo es una pintoresca masa de agua resguardada en el noroeste del Bosque de Elwynn, cerca de un huerto de frutales. Alimentado por una suave cascada bajo los acantilados de Ventormenta, su tranquila superficie oculta los peligros que acechan en sus orillas, desde bandidos Defias al acecho hasta extrañas perturbaciones en las líneas Ley locales. Situado bajo las imponentes murallas de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, el Lago Espejo debería ser un pacífico retiro para pescadores y viajeros cansados. En su lugar, los forajidos de la Hermandad Defias merodean por los huertos circundantes, convirtiendo cualquier estancia prolongada en un peligro para los lugareños que pasan por allí. Peor aún, las perturbaciones místicas por todo Azeroth han comenzado a distorsionar los canales naturales de energía arcana por todo el bosque. Los magos del Sagrario del Mago vigilan el lago con cautela y envían practicantes para tomar muestras de sus corrientes y asegurarse de que las comunidades río abajo no se envenenen con los vertidos arcanos caóticos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Initiates studying under the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind are dispatched here to gather water samples, learning firsthand how turbulent arcane channels can seep into the natural ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though close to the capital's towering walls, the lake stands as a reminder of how thinly stretched the kingdom's guards are against Defias outlaws."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Despite its scenic appearance, the area around the lake is heavily prowled by Defias bandits who target travelers and farmers. Additionally, the recent fluctuations in regional magic have prompted concerns about the lake's water safety.",["al"]={"is mirror lake safe","mirror lake enemies","defias mirror lake"},["q"]="Why is Mirror Lake dangerous?"},{["a"]="Massive magical conflicts across Azeroth have destabilized ley currents throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind. The Wizard's Sanctum dispatches initiates to sample the lake's water to test for unstable arcane residue before it can affect those who drink from it.",["al"]={"wizard sanctum mirror lake","mirror lake quest","magic in mirror lake"},["q"]="Why are mages studying Mirror Lake?"},{["a"]="The waterfall cascades down from the high cliffs and waterways flanking the perimeter of Stormwind City, feeding the lake before the water winds through the Elwynn river system.",["al"]={"mirror lake waterfall","water source mirror lake"},["q"]="Where does the waterfall at Mirror Lake come from?"}},["kw"]={"defias","elwynn forest","mirror lake","stormwind","waterfall","wizards sanctum"},["n"]="Mirror Lake",["s"]="Mirror Lake is a picturesque body of water tucked into northwestern Elwynn Forest near an orchard. Fed by a gentle waterfall beneath the cliffs of Stormwind, its tranquil surface belies the dangers lurking on its shores, from prowling Defias bandits to strange disruptions in the local ley lines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated beneath the towering ramparts of Stormwind City, Mirror Lake ought to be a peaceful retreat for fishermen and weary travelers. Instead, brigands of the Defias Brotherhood stalk the surrounding orchards, making any prolonged stay perilous for passing locals. Worse still, mystical disturbances across Azeroth have begun warping the natural channels of arcane energy throughout the forest. The mages of the Wizard's Sanctum keep a cautious eye on the lake, sending practitioners to sample its currents and ensure that downstream communities are not poisoned by chaotic arcane runoff.",["t"]="A Troubled Idyl"}}}}}
t["subzone:mirror-lake-orchard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,281,21.494.0,43.208.0,37.161.0,43.283.0,61.185.0",["h"]="61e298",["n"]="Vergel del Lago Espejo",["s"]="Vergel del Lago Espejo. El Vergel del Lago Espejo es una tranquila arboleda y cabaña situada en la orilla sur del Lago Espejo, en el oeste del Bosque de Elwynn. En su día fue una apacible granja cerca de las Cataratas del Trueno, pero ha caído en manos de los bandidos Defias, que se aprovechan de la campiña mientras los guardias de Ventormenta miran hacia otro lado. Escondido cerca de las aguas torrenciales de las Cataratas del Trueno, el Vergel del Lago Espejo fue en su momento una productiva granja que se beneficiaba de las aguas limpias del Lago Espejo. Hoy en día, la apacible cabaña se encuentra invadida, tomada por ladrones y forajidos oportunistas que portan los colores de la Hermandad Defias. Con las fuerzas militares del reino mermadas y el rey Varian Wrynn desaparecido, las propiedades rurales como este vergel se han convertido en presas fáciles para los forajidos que buscan asegurarse escondites por toda la campiña de Elwynn.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The orchard demonstrates classic Defias strategy: seizing defensible, overlooked properties near water and cliffs to monitor roads while evading city patrols.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the occupied orchard is another bitter sign of the Defias Brotherhood's bold expansion across the heartland of the kingdom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Defias bandits currently occupy Mirror Lake Orchard and the cottage alongside it. They have driven away whatever honest folk once tended the trees and now use the secluded grounds as a base in western Elwynn.",["al"]={"who is at mirror lake orchard","who lives here","orchard enemies"},["q"]="Who controls Mirror Lake Orchard right now?"},{["a"]="The orchard sits along the southern shore of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest, just east of Thunder Falls and north of the main road heading toward Westfall.",["al"]={"mirror lake orchard location","where is the orchard","find orchard elwynn"},["q"]="Where is Mirror Lake Orchard located?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's standing army is largely absent from rural Elwynn due to political deadlock and the mysterious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. With local garrisons shorthanded, distant farmsteads and orchards are frequently left to fend for themselves against the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"why are defias here","where are the guards"},["q"]="Why hasn't Stormwind reclaimed the orchard?"},{["a"]="Mirror Lake drains directly into Thunder Falls, placing the orchard just above the roaring cascade. Its secluded position near the cliffs makes it an ideal, defensible spot for bandits.",["al"]={"thunder falls connection","orchard and waterfall"},["q"]="What is the connection between the orchard and Thunder Falls?"}},["kw"]={"defias brotherhood","elwynn forest","mirror lake","mirror lake orchard","stormwind bandits","thunder falls"},["n"]="Mirror Lake Orchard",["s"]="Mirror Lake Orchard is a quiet grove and cottage nestled on the southern banks of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful homestead near Thunder Falls, it has fallen into the hands of Defias bandits who exploit the countryside while Stormwind's guards look elsewhere.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away near the cascading waters of Thunder Falls, Mirror Lake Orchard was once a productive farmstead benefiting from the clean waters of Mirror Lake. Today, the peaceful cottage sits overrun, claimed by opportunistic thieves and brigands flying the colors of the Defias Brotherhood. With the kingdom's military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn missing, rural properties like this orchard have become easy pickings for outlaws looking to secure hideouts across the Elwynn countryside.",["t"]="A Grove Under Seizure"}}}}}
t["subzone:molsen-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,268,18.458.0,29.243.0,26.164.0,15.174.0",["h"]="e77cfd",["n"]="La Granja de Molsen",["s"]="La Granja de Molsen. La Granja de Molsen es una hacienda abandonada ubicada en la región agrícola de Páramos de Poniente. Antaño una fértil tierra de cultivo que alimentaba a Ventormenta, ha quedado en ruinas tras el alzamiento de la Hermandad Defias y los acechantes gólems de la cosecha mecánicos que dejaron a su paso. Al igual que muchas haciendas de Páramos de Poniente, La Granja de Molsen es una víctima del abandono del reino y del levantamiento criminal. Cuando la Hermandad Defias tomó el control del campo, los granjeros locales fueron expulsados o sufrieron un destino peor, dejando atrás sus cultivos y edificios. Ahora, en lugar de jornaleros recolectando grano, hostiles Vigías de la cosecha mecánicos y forajidos errantes recorren los campos descuidados, convirtiendo la granja en un peligro para cualquiera que viaje por la provincia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The overgrown fields of Molsen Farm are a grim reminder of Stormwind's failing grasp on its rural territories and the pressing threat of the Defias Brotherhood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm was abandoned when the Defias Brotherhood swept across Westfall. Left without military protection from Stormwind, the homesteaders could not defend their land against bandits and rogue harvest golems, forcing them to flee their homes.",["al"]={"why is it empty","who lived here","what happened to molsen farm"},["q"]="Why is Molsen Farm abandoned?"},{["a"]="The fields are overrun by malfunctioning Harvest Watchers and outlaws aligned with the Defias Brotherhood. No lawful citizens currently occupy or work the property.",["al"]={"molsen farm enemies","who is at molsen farm"},["q"]="Who controls the farm now?"},{["a"]="The farm takes its name from the local family that originally settled and tilled the land before the recent unrest drove Westfall's agrarian population into exile or poverty.",["al"]={"who is molsen","molsen family"},["q"]="Who was Molsen?"}},["kw"]={"abandoned farm","defias","harvest watcher","homestead","molsen farm","westfall"},["n"]="Molsen Farm",["s"]="Molsen Farm is an abandoned homestead located in the breadbasket region of Westfall. Once a fertile piece of farmland feeding Stormwind, it has fallen into ruin following the rise of the Defias Brotherhood and the prowling mechanical harvest golems left in their wake.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Like many homesteads across Westfall, Molsen Farm stands as a casualty of the kingdom's neglect and criminal uprising. When the Defias Brotherhood took control of the countryside, the resident farmers were driven out or worse, abandoning their crops and buildings. Now, instead of laborers gathering grain, hostile mechanical Harvest Watchers and wandering outlaws scour the untended fields, making the farm a hazard to anyone traveling through the province.",["t"]="A Ruined Homestead"}}}}}
t["subzone:moonbrook"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,275,13.594.0,17.406.1,27.252.0,42.229.0,41.266.0,40.245.0",["h"]="1339dc",["n"]="Arroyo de la Luna",["s"]="Arroyo de la Luna. En su momento un bullicioso núcleo agrícola y pueblo minero en el suroeste de Páramos de Poniente, Arroyo de la Luna se alza hoy como un pueblo fantasma sin ley. La Hermandad Defias ha invadido por completo la localidad y la utiliza como pantalla fortificada para ocultar su cuartel general subterráneo en Las Minas de la Muerte. Antes de la Primera Guerra, Arroyo de la Luna era una comunidad vital en el centro del granero de Páramos de Poniente, que sustentaba a las familias de agricultores locales y los lucrativos pozos de oro de Las Minas de la Muerte. Aunque fue arrasado por la Horda Antigua y reconstruido minuciosamente tras la Segunda Guerra, su paz no duró mucho. Desatendido por la Cámara de los Nobles de Ventormenta y desprovisto de protección militar, el asentamiento no pudo resistir a la vengativa Hermandad de los Albañiles cuando huyeron a las tierras salvajes. Los bandidos expulsaron a los colonos honrados y obligaron tanto a ciudadanos como a maestros a huir hacia Colina del Centinela y el Bosque de Elwynn.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The alleys and ransacked homes of Moonbrook offer an unvarnished look at an entire outlaw syndicate operating in broad daylight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Moonbrook stands as a bitter reminder of the kingdom's neglect, where law-abiding subjects were abandoned to the Defias Brotherhood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Moonbrook was abandoned by its peaceful residents when the Defias Brotherhood seized control of Westfall. Without the Stormwind Army to garrison the region, the townsfolk were forced out, and the bandits claimed the entire town as their own stronghold.",["al"]={"what happened to moonbrook","why are there bandits in moonbrook","who took over moonbrook"},["q"]="Why is Moonbrook abandoned?"},{["a"]="The mine entrance beneath the barn on the edge of Moonbrook leads into the Deadmines. Once an immense source of gold for Stormwind, the labyrinthine tunnels are now the secret redoubt and staging ground of the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"where are deadmines","what is under moonbrook","moonbrook mine entrance"},["q"]="Where does the mine inside Moonbrook lead?"},{["a"]="Moonbrook was once populated by miners, farmers, and tradespeople who supported Westfall's agriculture. Notable former residents included Stalvan Mistmantle, who briefly served as the headmaster of the local Moonbrook Schoolhouse before the bandits overran the town.",["al"]={"moonbrook residents","who lived in moonbrook","stalvan mistmantle school"},["q"]="Who used to live here before the bandits?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's court has repeatedly refused to send royal troops to liberate Moonbrook or the surrounding farms, claiming resources are stretched thin. The local defense is left entirely to the volunteer People's Militia stationed at Sentinel Hill.",["al"]={"will stormwind save moonbrook","why doesn't the army help moonbrook"},["q"]="Does Stormwind plan to reclaim the town?"}},["kw"]={"deadmines","defias","moonbrook","schoolhouse","sentinel hill","vancleef","westfall"},["n"]="Moonbrook",["s"]="Once a bustling agricultural hub and mining town in southwestern Westfall, Moonbrook now stands as a lawless ghost town. The town has been completely overrun by the Defias Brotherhood, who use it as a fortified screen to hide their subterranean headquarters in the Deadmines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the First War, Moonbrook was a vital community at the center of Westfall's breadbasket, supporting local farming families and the lucrative gold shafts of the Deadmines. Though it was razed by the Old Horde and painstakingly rebuilt after the Second War, its peace did not last. Neglected by the House of Nobles in Stormwind and stripped of military protection, the settlement could not resist the vengeful Stonemasons Guild when they fled into the wilderness. Bandits drove out the honest homesteaders, forcing citizens and teachers alike to flee toward Sentinel Hill and Elwynn Forest.",["t"]="A Fallen Town"},{["b"]="Today, Moonbrook is effectively the surface garrison for Edwin VanCleef's rebellion. Red-masked thugs and rogue wizards patrol the streets and ransacked homes, while harvest golems patrol the surrounding weed-choked fields. The quiet residential streets conceal the entrance to the Deadmines beneath an unassuming barn on the town edge, making Moonbrook the most dangerous hotbed of treason in the kingdom.",["t"]="Defias Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:moonshrine-ruins"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,234,22.564.0,20.402.1,52.185.0,38.186.0,35.189.0,21.183.0",["h"]="be1850",["n"]="Ruinas del Santuario Lunar",["s"]="Ruinas del Santuario Lunar. Las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar son una extensión inundada de antigua arquitectura de los elfos de la noche en las profundidades de Cavernas de Brazanegra. En su día dedicadas al culto a Elune, estas salas en ruinas han sido profanadas y tomadas por el culto del Martillo Crepuscular. Más allá de la cavernosa Alberca de Ask'ar se encuentran las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar, un sombrío testimonio del antiguo pasado de los elfos de la noche en la costa de Vallefresno. Estas salas parcialmente sumergidas resonaron antaño con cánticos en honor a la Diosa de la Luna Elune, pero el Gran Cataclismo destrozó el templo e inundó sus niveles inferiores con agua de mar. Hoy en día, las aguas turbias bullen de bestias acuáticas salvajes, desde cangrejos agresivos hasta tresadones serpentinos, mientras que el culto del Martillo Crepuscular mantiene una presencia activa entre las piedras, entregado a oscuros rituales que se burlan del origen sagrado del santuario.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The binding of water spirits like Baron Aquanis via dark runestones reveals how deeply the Twilight's Hammer distorts and enslaves elemental forces.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing these sacred halls dedicated to Elune reduced to flooded, cult-infested ruins is a bitter grievance for any night elf journeying into the deeps."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The ruins were originally part of a grand underground temple complex dedicated to the night elven goddess Elune, constructed before the Great Sundering tore the ancient continent apart.",["al"]={"moonshrine origins","who built moonshrine ruins","what is this place"},["q"]="What were the Moonshrine Ruins originally built for?"},{["a"]="The ruins are infested with hostile aquatic beasts like threshadons and snapping crabs, alongside cultists belonging to the Twilight's Hammer, who have overrun the entire sunken complex.",["al"]={"who is here","moonshrine mobs","twilights hammer blackfathom"},["q"]="Who controls the Moonshrine Ruins now?"},{["a"]="The ruins lie past the tunnels beyond the Pool of Ask'ar. From the Moonshrine Ruins, pathways connect directly deeper toward the Moonshrine Sanctum and provide access to the Forgotten Pool.",["al"]={"moonshrine exits","where does this go","path through ruins"},["q"]="Where do the Moonshrine Ruins lead?"},{["a"]="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental summoned by touching a submerged runestone hidden in the murky water beneath the ruins, serving the sinister aims of the Twilight's Hammer.",["al"]={"baron aquanis lore","underwater boss moonshrine","elemental in water"},["q"]="Who is Baron Aquanis?"}},["kw"]={"aquanis","blackfathom","moonshrine","ruins","sanctum","threshadon","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Moonshrine Ruins",["s"]="The Moonshrine Ruins are a flooded expanse of ancient night elven architecture deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Once dedicated to the worship of Elune, these crumbling halls have been desecrated and seized by the Twilight's Hammer cult.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Past the cavernous Pool of Ask'ar lies the Moonshrine Ruins, a somber testament to the night elves' ancient past along the Ashenvale coast. These partially submerged halls once rang with chants honoring the Moon Goddess Elune, but the Great Sundering shattered the temple and drowned its lower levels in sea water. Today, the murky waters churn with feral aquatic beasts, from aggressive crabs to serpentine threshadons, while the Twilight's Hammer cult maintains an active presence throughout the stones, bent on dark rituals that mock the shrine's sacred origin.",["t"]="Flooded Halls of Elune"},{["b"]="Connecting directly toward the Forgotten Pool and the Moonshrine Sanctum, the ruins serve as a staging ground for the cult's summonings. Beneath the surface of the flooded chambers sits an ancient runestone bound to the elements. Through this aquatic focus, the Twilight's Hammer manipulates the waters of the deeps, calling forth Baron Aquanis, a monstrous water elemental bound to their dark designs.",["t"]="The Elemental Depths"}}}}}
t["subzone:mor-shan-rampart"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,318,17.523.0,15.337.0,29.205.0,32.173.0,55.251.0,55.172.0",["h"]="a88fdd",["n"]="La Muralla de Mor'shan",["s"]="La Muralla de Mor'shan. La Muralla de Mor'shan es una barricada de la Horda fuertemente fortificada situada en la frontera norte de Los Baldíos, que custodia la entrada a Vallefresno. Construida principalmente por el Clan Grito de Guerra, protege el territorio de la Horda frente a los contraataques de los elfos de la noche y sirve al mismo tiempo como base de operaciones para incursiones más profundas en el bosque. Erguida en el extremo norte del Camino del Oro, la Muralla de Mor'shan marca la transición entre las áridas llanuras de Los Baldíos y el dosel ancestral de Vallefresno. Levantado con maderos pesados, empalizadas defensivas y torres de vigilancia fortificadas, este baluarte se erigió para contener las represalias de las fuerzas de los elfos de la noche, indignadas por las operaciones de tala de la Horda. Funciona tanto de escudo que asegura la puerta norte hacia el interior de Kalimdor como de puesto de avanzada para partidas de asalto que avanzan hacia el norte, en dirección a Astranaar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance fighters view the Mor'shan Rampart as an aggressive barricade erected by Horde lumber operations to protect stolen territory and stage raids into Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the Rampart is the primary overland gate protecting the heart of the Barrens from night elf incursions, while keeping the supply lines to Ashenvale's logging operations intact."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a fortified Horde border post situated where the Barrens meets Ashenvale. It was constructed to block Alliance counterattacks from entering the Barrens and to guard the northern end of the Gold Road.",["al"]={"morshan rampart","what is this barricade","northern barrens gate"},["q"]="What is the Mor'shan Rampart?"},{["a"]="The fortification is garrisoned by the Horde, specifically warriors and sentries tied to the Warsong clan. They maintain watchtowers and palisades along the forest boundary.",["al"]={"who holds morshan","who guards the rampart","morshan defenders"},["q"]="Who controls this fortification?"},{["a"]="It anchors the northern terminus of the Gold Road, making it the primary land route connecting the central Barrens with Ashenvale. Controlling this chokepoint ensures that night elf strikes cannot easily sweep south into the heart of Horde-held lands.",["al"]={"why build ramparts here","strategic importance morshan"},["q"]="Why is the rampart here instead of deeper in Ashenvale?"},{["a"]="No. The rampart is an active Horde military position. Alliance travelers approaching from either Ashenvale or the Barrens will be attacked on sight by the stationed guards.",["al"]={"can alliance pass","alliance crossing morshan"},["q"]="Can Alliance travelers pass through the rampart safely?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","barrens","gold road","mor'shan rampart","morshan","warsong clan","warsong outriders"},["n"]="Mor'shan Rampart",["s"]="The Mor'shan Rampart is a heavily fortified Horde barricade positioned at the northern border of the Barrens, guarding the entrance to Ashenvale. Constructed primarily by the Warsong clan, it shields Horde territory from night elf counterattacks while serving as a staging ground for incursions deeper into the forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing at the northern terminus of the Gold Road, the Mor'shan Rampart marks the transition between the arid plains of the Barrens and the ancient canopies of Ashenvale. Built from heavy timber, defensive palisades, and fortified watchtowers, this bulwark was raised to stem the retaliatory strikes of night elven forces outraged by the Horde's logging operations. It acts both as a shield securing the northern gate to Kalimdor's interior and as a forward staging post for raiding parties pushing north toward Astranaar.",["t"]="The Northern Gate"},{["b"]="Manned primarily by battle-hardened fighters affiliated with the Warsong clan, the rampart remains under constant military readiness. From these parapets, sentries monitor the tree line for night elf scouts and archers, keeping open supply lines between the frontline outposts of Ashenvale and the greater Horde settlements to the south.",["t"]="Warsong Outpost"}}}}}
t["subzone:mystic-ward"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,406,32.715.0,33.214.0,45.179.0,43.248.0,32.174.0",["h"]="dcdada",["n"]="Sala Mística",["s"]="Sala Mística. La Sala Mística es el distrito noroccidental de Forjaz, que sirve como el tranquilo santuario de la capital enana para la devoción espiritual y el estudio arcano. Distinguible por sus estandartes de color azul pálido y sus silenciosas salas, contrasta enormemente con el resonar de los yunques de la cercana Gran Fundición. Su estructura más imponente, la Sala de los Misterios, reúne a sacerdotes, paladines y magos bajo cavernosos arcos de piedra. Aunque los enanos son famosos en todo Azeroth por su destreza en la forja y en el campo de batalla, la Sala Mística representa las actividades intelectuales y espirituales más sosegadas del reino. Marcado por una heráldica de color azul pálido, este cavernoso barrio conecta el Distrito Comercial con la Caverna Abandonada y la Gran Fundición. En sus inmediaciones, los comerciantes abastecen a eruditos y tejedores de hechizos con vestimentas, pergaminos y componentes alquímicos en tiendas como El Mago Combatiente y Vestimentas Místicas de Maeva. Dominando el distrito se alza la majestuosa Sala de los Misterios, donde las disciplinas sagradas de la Luz Sagrada se cruzan con las artes practicadas de la magia arcana, ofreciendo guía a quienes blanden poderes invisibles en defensa de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="For Alliance spellweavers, the Mystic Ward serves as the premier center in Khaz Modan for arcane supplies, spell tomes, and advanced study outside the academies of Stormwind.",["class:Priest"]="The ward and its grand Hall of Mysteries provide a peaceful haven where dwarven and visiting practitioners of the Holy Light gather for prayer, guidance, and communion."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Mystic Ward is Ironforge's dedicated district for arcane magic, scholarly research, and spiritual worship. It provides spellcaster supplies, reagent shops, and training grounds for paladins, priests, and mages.",["al"]={"purpose of mystic ward","what happens here","mystic ward role"},["q"]="What is the Mystic Ward used for?"},{["a"]="The district is anchored by the Hall of Mysteries, a grand vaulted chamber housing the capital's trainers for holy and arcane spellcasters, as well as a prominent ornamental pool.",["al"]={"hall of mysteries","big temple","mystic ward building"},["q"]="What is the main building in the Mystic Ward?"},{["a"]="Ironforge uses distinct heraldry to delineate its city districts. While the Military Ward flies martial red and the Great Forge features fiery orange, the Mystic Ward displays pale blue banners to symbolize contemplation, wisdom, and magical study.",["al"]={"blue banners ironforge","why blue flags"},["q"]="Why are the banners in this ward pale blue?"},{["a"]="The ward sits in the northwestern quadrant of the city. Passages connect it south toward the Commons, southeast to the Great Forge, and east directly into the Forlorn Cavern.",["al"]={"mystic ward connections","how to get to mystic ward"},["q"]="Where does the Mystic Ward lead?"}},["kw"]={"hall of mysteries","ironforge","longberrys reagents","maevas mystical apparel","mage trainer","mystic ward","priest trainer","the fighting wizard"},["n"]="Mystic Ward",["s"]="The Mystic Ward is the northwestern district of Ironforge, serving as the dwarven capital's quiet sanctuary for spiritual devotion and arcane study. Distinguishable by its cool, pale blue banners and quiet halls, it stands in stark contrast to the clanging anvils of the nearby Great Forge. Its grandest structure, the Hall of Mysteries, gathers priests, paladins, and mages beneath cavernous stone arches.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While dwarves are famed across Azeroth for their prowess at the forge and on the battlefield, the Mystic Ward represents the kingdom's quieter intellectual and spiritual pursuits. Marked by pale blue heraldry, this cavernous quarter connects the bustling Commons to the Forlorn Cavern and the Great Forge. Within its reaches, merchants supply scholars and spellweavers with regalia, scrolls, and alchemical reagents from shops like The Fighting Wizard and Maeva's Mystical Apparel. Dominating the district is the majestic Hall of Mysteries, where the holy disciplines of the Holy Light intersect with the practiced arts of arcane magic, offering guidance to those who wield unseen powers in defense of the Alliance.",["t"]="A Sanctuary of Faith and Sorcery"}}}}}
t["subzone:north-coast"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,272,20.385.0,18.410.0,39.165.0,12.119.0,46.192.0,51.162.0",["h"]="459abd",["n"]="La Costa Norte",["s"]="La Costa Norte. La Costa Norte es un tramo de litoral desolado y envuelto en niebla que marca el extremo septentrional de los Claros de Tirisfal a lo largo del Mare Magnum. Corrompidas por la caída de Lordaeron, las frías playas están repletas de fauna marina en descomposición y son defendidas con ferocidad por tribus de múrlocs hostiles. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, estas aguas norteñas y playas pedregosas formaban parte de la pacífica frontera norte de Lordaeron. Cuando la Plaga de la No-Muerte arrasó el continente, su añublo corruptor se filtró por los acantilados y envenenó la costa. Las aguas se volvieron gélidas y turbias, arrastrando a la orilla los cadáveres de criaturas marinas gigantescas que ahora se pudren sobre la arena entre la perenne niebla costera.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="While Forsaken patrol routes cling to the road through Brill, clearing the North Coast of encroaching murlocs ensures the northern flank of Tirisfal Glades remains relatively secure."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The beach is primarily occupied by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs, their tadpoles, and scavengers picking at the rotting sea life that washes ashore from the Great Sea.",["al"]={"north coast mobs","what lives on north coast","monsters north coast"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the North Coast?"},{["a"]="Deeb is an individual murloc who can be found lingering along the North Coast among the huts and shallows of the shore.",["al"]={"deeb","murloc deeb","who is deeb"},["q"]="Who is Deeb?"},{["a"]="The Plague of Undeath that devastated Lordaeron seeped into the coastal ecology, poisoning the surrounding shallows and causing dead marine beasts to wash ashore to decay on the blighted sand.",["al"]={"dead sea monsters","beached whales tirisfal","why dead creatures"},["q"]="Why is the coast covered in rotting carcasses?"},{["a"]="Neither the Forsaken nor any remnants of the Alliance actively garrison the North Coast. It remains a wild, untamed fringe left largely to murlocs and sea vermin.",["al"]={"who owns north coast","forsaken presence north coast"},["q"]="Is the North Coast contested by any major factions?"}},["kw"]={"beach","deeb","great sea","murloc","north coast","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},["n"]="North Coast",["s"]="The North Coast is a bleak, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline marking the northern edge of Tirisfal Glades along the Great Sea. Tainted by the fall of Lordaeron, the cold beaches are littered with rotting marine life and aggressively defended by tribes of hostile murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, these northern waters and stony beaches were part of the peaceful northern boundary of Lordaeron. When the Plague of Undeath swept across the continent, its corrupting blight seeped down the bluffs and poisoned the coast. The waters turned chill and murky, washing up the carcasses of giant sea creatures that now rot upon the sand amid the perennial coastal fog.",["t"]="A Blighted Shoreline"},{["b"]="With the human kingdom shattered and the Forsaken focusing their attention around Brill and the Capital City, coastal murlocs claimed the desolate sands. The local Vile Fin tribe maintains huts along the surf, utilizing nearby shallows as spawning grounds. Swarms of ravenous murlocs, including notable figures like Deeb and numerous growing tadpoles, violently guard the tideline against any surface-dwellers.",["t"]="The Vile Fin Shore"}}}}}
t["subzone:north-gate-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,261,18.469.0,36.233.0,42.175.0,49.223.0",["h"]="07669a",["n"]="Avanzada de la Puerta Norte",["s"]="Avanzada de la Puerta Norte. La Avanzada de la Puerta Norte es un campamento enano fortificado situado en lo alto del Paso de la Puerta Norte de Dun Morogh. Al vigilar la escarpada ruta entre el nevado corazón de Forjaz y Loch Modan, sus montaces protegen a los viajeros de la fauna hostil que infesta los riscos. Situado en mitad del Paso de la Puerta Norte, este pequeño asentamiento sirve como el umbral nororiental de Dun Morogh. Los montaces enanos apostados aquí mantienen el camino principal despejado de bestias al acecho y vigilan el tráfico que se dirige a través de los túneles montañosos hacia Loch Modan. El clima riguroso y los empinados barrancos hacen que las patrullas sean traicioneras, y la guarnición a menudo recurre a los viajeros para explorar las crestas circundantes en busca de patrullas desaparecidas y peligrosos depredadores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="The outpost showcases the stoic duty of Ironforge's Mountaineers, who hold the harsh highland passes open regardless of freezing weather or prowling predators.",["race:Gnome"]="Having resettled across Dun Morogh, gnomes often lend their wits and marksmanship to assist the dwarven garrison in tracking down lost patrols."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It serves as a mountain military checkpoint that secures North Gate Pass, the northern roadway connecting Dun Morogh to Loch Modan. Mountaineers stationed here keep the pass open to trade and travel by curbing wild beast populations.",["al"]={"north gate outpost purpose","why is north gate outpost here"},["q"]="What is North Gate Outpost used for?"},{["a"]="Traveling east through the mountain tunnels beyond the outpost leads into the temperate valley of Loch Modan, while heading west leads back down toward Kharanos and Ironforge.",["al"]={"where does north gate pass go","road past north gate outpost"},["q"]="Where does the road through the pass lead?"},{["a"]="The local wildlife along the snowy cliffs is fiercely territorial. Several mountaineers have gone missing into the crags while hunting dangerous beasts, forcing the garrison to enlist capable scouts to discover their fates.",["al"]={"north gate outpost quests","missing mountaineers"},["q"]="Why do the mountaineers need help from travelers?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineers","north gate outpost","north gate pass"},["n"]="North Gate Outpost",["s"]="North Gate Outpost is a fortified dwarven camp situated high in the North Gate Pass of Dun Morogh. Manning the rugged route between Ironforge's snowy heartland and Loch Modan, its mountaineers guard travelers against the hostile wildlife that infests the crags.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned in the middle of North Gate Pass, this small settlement serves as the northeastern threshold of Dun Morogh. Dwarven mountaineers stationed here keep the main roadway cleared of prowling beasts and monitor traffic heading through the mountain tunnels into Loch Modan. The harsh climate and steep ravines make patrol duty treacherous, and the garrison frequently calls upon travelers to scout the surrounding ridges for missing patrols and dangerous predators.",["t"]="Guards of the Pass"}}}}}
t["subzone:north-gate-pass"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,332,25.629.0,32.231.0,21.178.0,42.212.0",["h"]="832ab4",["n"]="Paso de la Puerta Norte",["s"]="Paso de la Puerta Norte. El Paso de la Puerta Norte es una vía montañosa vital que conecta los riscos nevados de Dun Morogh con la ondulada cuenca de Loch Modan. Forma el corredor septentrional a través de los picos de Khaz Modan, vigilado por una avanzada enana fortificada. Los viajeros que se dirigen hacia las tierras bajas del norte de Los Humedales recorren con frecuencia este camino de gran altitud. Tallado en la roca escarpada de Khaz Modan, el Paso de la Puerta Norte sirve como el enlace arterial septentrional entre los altos y helados valles de Dun Morogh y las templadas aguas de Loch Modan. Al descender a través de empinados túneles de montaña, los viajeros que emergen del oeste son recibidos por la amplia extensión del valle del lago. Debido a que se encuentra a poca distancia de los caminos que descienden hacia Los Humedales, el paso soporta un intenso tráfico de mensajeros enanos, comerciantes y aventureros errantes. Su valor estratégico está afianzado por la Avanzada de la Puerta Norte, donde los montañeros mantienen una vigilancia constante frente a los troggs y los depredadores de las montañas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The pass represents a crucial military and supply corridor connecting the dwarven capital to northern Alliance expeditions bound for the Wetlands.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves journeying between the high gates of Ironforge and the frontier settlements around The Loch, the pass is a familiar, stone-hewn threshold guarded by fellow mountaineers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The pass connects eastern Dun Morogh to northwestern Loch Modan. Following the road further north around the loch leads toward the mountain tunnels descending into the Wetlands, making it a critical junction for northern travelers.",["al"]={"where does north gate pass go","north gate pass destination","path through north gate pass"},["q"]="Where does North Gate Pass lead?"},{["a"]="The Ironforge Mountaineers maintain North Gate Outpost directly along the road, monitoring travelers and keeping the mountain passage clear of prowling beasts and roaming troggs.",["al"]={"who guards north gate pass","north gate pass guards","dwarf outpost north gate"},["q"]="What guards the pass?"},{["a"]="Both passes link Dun Morogh to Loch Modan through carved tunnels, but North Gate Pass lies to the north, offering the most direct overland route for travelers moving onward toward the Wetlands and northern lands.",["al"]={"difference north and south gate pass","north gate vs south gate"},["q"]="How does this differ from South Gate Pass?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineers","north gate outpost","north gate pass","wetlands"},["n"]="North Gate Pass",["s"]="North Gate Pass is a vital mountain thoroughfare connecting the snowy crags of Dun Morogh with the rolling basin of Loch Modan. It forms the northern corridor through the Khaz Modan peaks, watched over by a fortified dwarven outpost. Travelers heading toward the northern lowlands of the Wetlands frequently traverse this high road.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the sheer stone of Khaz Modan, North Gate Pass serves as the northern arterial link between the high, frozen valleys of Dun Morogh and the temperate waters of Loch Modan. Descending through steep mountain tunnels, travelers emerging from the west are greeted by the broad expanse of the loch valley. Because it sits within easy striking distance of the paths heading down into the Wetlands, the pass carries heavy traffic of dwarven messengers, merchants, and roaming adventurers. Its strategic value is anchored by the North Gate Outpost, where mountaineers keep vigilant watch against troggs and mountain predators.",["t"]="Gateway Between the Peaks"}}}}}
t["subzone:north-tide-s-hollow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,263,16.462.0,25.309.0,29.160.0,43.110.0,43.253.0,37.140.0",["h"]="275957",["n"]="Hoya Mareanorte",["s"]="Hoya Mareanorte. Hoya Mareanorte es un agreste rincón salvaje en el Bosque de Argénteos situado justo al norte de El Sepulcro. Acechado por huargen Furia Lunar feroces y leales al archimago renegado Arugal, el claro sirve como base de operaciones para las bestias que merodean por los bosques costeros. Escondida entre la densa arboleda al norte del asentamiento Renegado de El Sepulcro, Hoya Mareanorte está dominada por la salvaje manada Furia Lunar. Estos huargen feroces, traídos a Lordaeron mediante la temeraria hechicería del archimago Arugal, han establecido toscos campamentos por toda la hoya. Construidos únicamente con lo estrictamente necesario para estas resistentes bestias, estos toscos refugios proporcionan una base avanzada peligrosamente cerca de las rutas de viaje de los Renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="Positioned uncomfortably close to the Sepulcher, the Moonrage pack in North Tide's Hollow poses an immediate threat to Forsaken sovereignty and logistical lines in Silverpine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="North Tide's Hollow is located in western Silverpine Forest, situated just to the north of the Forsaken outpost known as the Sepulcher, near the coastal bluffs.",["al"]={"north tides hollow location","where is north tides hollow","hollow location"},["q"]="Where is North Tide's Hollow?"},{["a"]="The hollow is infested with Moonrage worgen, supernatural wolf-beasts bound to the madness of Archmage Arugal.",["al"]={"who lives here","north tides hollow enemies","mobs in north tides hollow"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit North Tide's Hollow?"},{["a"]="While worgen are vicious and wild, the Moonrage pack retains enough cunning to organize basic encampments. Being naturally resilient and hardened, they require only the most primitive shelters and survival necessities to endure the Lordaeron wilderness.",["al"]={"worgen camps","why do worgen have tents"},["q"]="Why do the worgen live in crude camps here?"},{["a"]="The Moonrage worgen in North Tide's Hollow serve Archmage Arugal, who summoned worgen into Lordaeron and commands them from Shadowfang Keep.",["al"]={"who leads the worgen","worgen master"},["q"]="Who controls the worgen in this area?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","beachhead","moonrage","north tide's hollow","sepulcher","silverpine forest","worgen"},["n"]="North Tide's Hollow",["s"]="North Tide's Hollow is a rugged wilderness pocket in Silverpine Forest located just north of the Sepulcher. Haunted by feral Moonrage worgen loyal to the rogue Archmage Arugal, the clearing serves as a base of operations for the beasts stalking the coastal woods.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the dense timber north of the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher, North Tide's Hollow is dominated by the savage Moonrage pack. These feral worgen, brought into Lordaeron through the reckless sorcery of Archmage Arugal, have established crude encampments throughout the hollow. Built with only the barest necessities required by the hardy beasts, these rough shelters provide a forward staging ground dangerously close to Forsaken travel routes.",["t"]="A Feral Foothold"},{["b"]="Unlike ordinary wilderness predators, the worgen of North Tide's Hollow answer to the sinister will emanating from Shadowfang Keep. Their proximity to both the western shoreline and the main road through Silverpine makes them a constant menace to Forsaken couriers and patrols attempting to secure the region.",["t"]="Under Shadowfang's Shadow"}}}}}
t["subzone:north-tide-s-run"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,282,24.412.0,22.304.0,25.178.0,25.150.0,39.219.0,37.164.0",["h"]="1072bd",["n"]="Cala Mareanorte",["s"]="Cala Mareanorte. Cala Mareanorte es la costa noroccidental de Bosque de Argénteos, azotada por el viento y bordeando la orilla del Mare Magnum. Marcado por una solitaria fogata y un naufragio semisumergido, este tramo de arena es conocido como un aislado terreno de pruebas para los druidas viajeros que buscan la armonía con las aguas. Extendiéndose a lo largo del extremo noroccidental de Bosque de Argénteos, Cala Mareanorte se compone de arena fría, un oleaje constante y una franja del Mare Magnum. Su punto de referencia más inconfundible es un barco naufragado parcialmente sumergido, inclinado de forma precaria en los bajíos cercanos a la playa. Aparte de los restos del naufragio, la única señal de presencia humana es una humilde fogata atendida por Wallace el Ciego, quien mantiene una tranquila vigilia junto al romper de la marea.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, this cold coast represents a vital rite of passage, housing the submerged trial components necessary to master the sea lion form.",["race:Tauren"]="Far from the warm plains of Mulgore, North Tide's Run is one of the few places in Lordaeron that young tauren travel to early in their spiritual journeys."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the northwestern shoreline and coastal shelf of Silverpine Forest, bordered by the Great Sea. It is characterized by its sunken ship, tidal waters, and bleak, quiet strand.",["al"]={"north tides run","where is north tides run","what is this beach"},["q"]="What is North Tide's Run?"},{["a"]="Wallace the Blind is a hermit who has pitched a small camp and fire right at the water's edge along the beach, sitting quietly near the sunken vessel.",["al"]={"wallace blind","wallace the blind silverpine","who is the guy at the fire"},["q"]="Who is Wallace the Blind?"},{["a"]="Tauren druids travel here on pilgrimage during their trials to commune with the spirits of the sea. By braving the depths near the shoreline to recover lost pendant fragments, they earn the power to assume aquatic form.",["al"]={"druid quest silverpine beach","aquatic form silverpine","why tauren here"},["q"]="Why do druids come to North Tide's Run?"},{["a"]="The wreck is a partially submerged vessel resting in the shallows just off the sand. Its presence serves as a navigational landmark for travelers combing the coast.",["al"]={"shipwreck north tides run","sunken boat silverpine beach","ship wreck"},["q"]="What is the sunken ship in the water?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","druid trial","great sea","north tide's run","shipwreck","silverpine forest","wallace the blind"},["n"]="North Tide's Run",["s"]="North Tide's Run is the windswept northwestern shoreline of Silverpine Forest, skirting the edge of the Great Sea. Marked by a lonely campfire and a half-sunken shipwreck, this stretch of sand is known as a secluded trial ground for traveling druids seeking harmony with the waters.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching along the northwest edge of Silverpine Forest, North Tide's Run consists of cold sand, pounding surf, and a strip of the Great Sea. Its most unmistakable landmark is a partially submerged shipwreck tilted precariously in the shallows near the beach. Aside from the wreckage, the only sign of habitation is a humble campfire tended by Wallace the Blind, who keeps a quiet vigil beside the lapping tide.",["t"]="A Lonely Coastal Outpost"},{["b"]="Despite its bleak atmosphere, North Tide's Run holds sacred importance for Horde initiates walking the path of Cenarius. Young tauren druids are directed here on pilgrimage to recover underwater relics lost to the waves, testing their lung capacity and endurance to earn the blessing of the aquatic form.",["t"]="Waters of the Sea Lion"}}}}}
t["subzone:northshire-abbey"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="La Hermandad de Villanorte es una orden religiosa de clérigos, sacerdotes y paladines con base en la Abadía de Villanorte. Fundada originalmente hace siglos por clérigos misioneros de Lordaeron, fue restablecida por el arzobispo Alonsus Faol tras la Primera Guerra para entrenar a devotos defensores y preservar las sagradas escrituras.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="56b216",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Durante la Primera Guerra, la abadía poseía una importancia estratégica y espiritual para Ventormenta. Las fuerzas orcas incitaron a bandidos humanos a atacarla y, tras mantener cautiva brevemente allí a la semiorca Garona, una embestida masiva de la Horda arrasó el recinto sagrado. Permaneció en ruinas durante toda la guerra hasta que la Alianza expulsó a los clanes orcos y la reconstruyó.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="c273bf",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El ejército de Ventormenta está disperso protegiendo fronteras lejanas, dejando las regiones periféricas escasamente vigiladas. Los oportunistas kóbold han infestado las minas de oro locales, mientras que la Hermandad Defias aprovecha las brechas para asaltar a los viajeros, acosar los viñedos locales y saquear la biblioteca de la abadía en busca de tomos arcanos y reliquias sagradas.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e9582e",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Durante la Primera Guerra, un cabecilla ogro llamado Turok robó el sagrado Libro de la Divinidad de la Abadía de Villanorte y se refugió en Las Minas de la Muerte. Sir Anduin Lothar encabezó una expedición a las profundidades para recuperar las sagradas escrituras, quedando atrapado hasta que un grupo de rescate real lo salvó y devolvió el tomo a la custodia de la abadía.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="a770b9",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="16,322,26.656.0,20.618.0,38.314.0,52.351.0,59.321.0,66.320.0",["h"]="b6ded6",["n"]="Abadía de Villanorte",["s"]="Abadía de Villanorte. La Abadía de Villanorte es un monasterio histórico enclavado en el Valle de Villanorte, en las estribaciones septentrionales del Bosque de Elwynn. Reconstruida tras su destrucción en la Primera Guerra, sirve como el corazón espiritual de la Hermandad de Villanorte y como centro de adiestramiento principal para los nuevos defensores que responden a la llamada del reino de Ventormenta. Siglos atrás, clérigos procedentes de Lordaeron viajaron al sur, al reino de Ventormenta, para difundir el culto a la Luz Sagrada, fundando la Sagrada Orden de los Clérigos de Villanorte y su abadía. El monasterio no tardó en convertirse en un pilar de la vida del reino, atendiendo a los enfermos e incluso cuidando del joven Guardián Medivh durante sus años en coma. Durante la Primera Guerra, la abadía sufrió constantes asaltos a manos de bandidos y de la Horda orca, que culminaron en su absoluta destrucción. Cuando la Alianza de Lordaeron liberó la región en la Segunda Guerra, el arzobispo Alonsus Faol ayudó a reconstruir el santuario, refundando a sus protectores bajo el nombre de Hermandad de Villanorte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Northshire represents the legacy of Archbishop Alonsus Faol and the early clerics whose sacrifices laid the foundation for the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Northshire Abbey is the cradle of your journey, where the kingdom's history of resilience and devotion welcomes every recruit taking up arms."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Brotherhood of Northshire is a religious order of clerics, priests, and paladins based out of Northshire Abbey. Originally founded centuries ago by missioning clerics from Lordaeron, it was re-established by Archbishop Alonsus Faol after the First War to train faithful defenders and preserve sacred scripture.",["al"]={"who runs northshire abbey","northshire clerics","brotherhood of northshire lore"},["q"]="What is the Brotherhood of Northshire?"},{["a"]="During the First War, the abbey held strategic and spiritual importance for Stormwind. Orcish forces incited human brigands to attack it, and after the half-orc Garona was briefly held captive there, a massive Horde onslaught leveled the holy grounds. It remained ruined throughout the war until the Alliance drove out the orcish clans and rebuilt it.",["al"]={"who destroyed northshire abbey","northshire first war","what happened to northshire"},["q"]="Why was Northshire Abbey destroyed in the First War?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's military is stretched thin protecting distant borders, leaving outlying regions poorly guarded. Opportunistic kobolds have infested the local gold mines, while the Defias Brotherhood exploits the gaps to rob travelers, harass the local vineyards, and raid the abbey's library for arcane tomes and holy relics.",["al"]={"why is northshire under attack","kobolds in northshire","defias outside northshire"},["q"]="Why are there Defias bandits and kobolds outside the abbey?"},{["a"]="During the First War, an ogre chieftain named Turok stole the sacred Tome of Divinity from Northshire Abbey and retreated into the Deadmines. Sir Anduin Lothar led an expedition into the depths to recover the holy scripture, getting trapped until a royal rescue party saved him and returned the tome to the abbey's care.",["al"]={"tome of divinity northshire","northshire deadmines lore","anduin lothar deadmines"},["q"]="What is the connection between Northshire Abbey and the Deadmines?"}},["kw"]={"abbey","brotherhood","clerics","defias","elwynn","faol","northshire","valley"},["n"]="Northshire Abbey",["s"]="Northshire Abbey is a historic monastery nestled in Northshire Valley within the northern foothills of Elwynn Forest. Rebuilt after its destruction in the First War, it serves as the spiritual heart of the Brotherhood of Northshire and a premier training center for new defenders answering the kingdom of Stormwind's call.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Centuries ago, clerics from Lordaeron traveled south into the kingdom of Stormwind to spread the worship of the Holy Light, establishing the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics and their abbey. The monastery quickly became an anchor of kingdom life, caring for the sick and even tending to the young Guardian Medivh during his years in a coma. During the First War, the abbey suffered repeated assaults by brigands and the Orcish Horde, culminating in its utter destruction. When the Alliance of Lordaeron liberated the region in the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol helped rebuild the sanctuary, refounding its protectors as the Brotherhood of Northshire.",["t"]="A Legacy of Faith and Ruin"},{["b"]="Today, Northshire Abbey functions as the starting ground for volunteers, militia recruits, and novices seeking to defend a beleaguered Stormwind. Split into the Main Hall, Hall of Arms, and Library Wing, it houses instructors in the martial, arcane, and holy arts, while scouts and rogues train in the outer yards. Despite the watchful presence of the Knights of the Silver Hand, peace here remains precarious. Kobolds overrun nearby mines, aggressive wolves roam the orchards, and agents of the Defias Brotherhood stalk the valley roads, pilfering ancient scrolls and sacred librams from the abbey's storied archives.",["t"]="The Training Grounds"}}}}}
t["subzone:northshire-valley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,423,20.635.0,20.549.0,44.358.0,49.250.0,42.256.0,44.204.0,50.196.0,35.215.0",["h"]="961b3e",["n"]="Valle de Villanorte",["s"]="Valle de Villanorte. Escondido en las montañas septentrionales del Bosque de Elwynn, el Valle de Villanorte sirve como cuna pacífica y campo de entrenamiento para los nuevos defensores del reino de Ventormenta. Rodeado de barreras naturales, alberga la histórica Abadía de Villanorte, fértiles viñedos y la rica Mina del Eco. A pesar de su apariencia tranquila, el valle se enfrenta a una creciente agitación provocada por bandidos rebeldes, plagas de kóbold y depredadores desplazados. El Valle de Villanorte está delimitado por crestas montañosas casi infranqueables, con su único camino en dirección sur a través de un cuerpo de guardia fortificado hacia Villadorada y el resto del Bosque de Elwynn. Un río de aguas cristalinas serpentea por sus pastos antes de desembocar al sur en el Lago de Cristal. En el corazón del valle se alza la Abadía de Villanorte, un antiguo santuario donde se enseña la Luz Sagrada y donde los reclutas son instruidos por los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata y veteranos experimentados. Más allá de los muros de la abadía se extienden los pródigos Viñedos de Villanorte y la Mina del Eco, conformando un reducto autosuficiente del territorio de Ventormenta que parece muy alejado de las guerras del resto del mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Northshire serves as a crucial recruitment and recovery station for the Grand Alliance, training the next generation of defenders to stabilize the heart of the kingdom.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Northshire Valley is the place where their journey begins, stepping into the abbey's grounds to answer the call of a kingdom in need."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The valley contains Northshire Abbey, a key spiritual hub and training ground for Stormwind's forces, as well as crucial local resources like Echo Ridge Mine and the vineyards. With Stormwind's military stretched thin, Marshal McBride maintains a guarded gate at the southern pass to prevent threats from leaking between the valley and greater Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"why guards northshire","gate in northshire","who protects northshire"},["q"]="Why is Northshire Valley so heavily guarded?"},{["a"]="Deputy Willem notes that packs of wolves have recently surged across the river, having fled into the valley from the darkened forests of Duskwood to the south. The darkness spreading in Duskwood has driven wild beasts into normally tranquil pastures.",["al"]={"why so many wolves","wolf infestation","wolves from duskwood"},["q"]="Where did all the wolves in the valley come from?"},{["a"]="Kobolds are opportunistic burrowers drawn to underground mineral veins. As kingdom patrols grew thin, a clan of kobolds took advantage of the lack of protection to claim Echo Ridge Mine for its gold and candles, forcing the human miners out of the tunnels.",["al"]={"echo ridge kobolds","why kobolds in northshire","kobold problem"},["q"]="Why are kobolds attacking Echo Ridge Mine?"},{["a"]="The thieves operating near Milly Osworth's vineyard are agents of the Defias Brotherhood. They prey on the outskirts of the valley to disrupt supplies, harass local farmers, and test the abbey's defenses.",["al"]={"vineyard bandits","defias in northshire","red mask thugs"},["q"]="Who are the bandits harassing the vineyards?"},{["a"]="During the Second War, Northshire Abbey fell into enemy hands and was briefly utilized as a headquarters by Cho'gall's Twilight's Hammer clan before the Alliance reclaimed and restored the valley.",["al"]={"northshire second war","twilight hammer northshire","chogall northshire"},["q"]="What happened to Northshire during the Second War?"},{["a"]="The only passable exit on foot is the southern road leading through the guarded gatehouse. Passing through this gate takes travelers directly into central Elwynn Forest, pointing down the main road toward Goldshire.",["al"]={"exit northshire","path to goldshire","how to leave"},["q"]="How do you leave Northshire Valley?"}},["kw"]={"abbey","defias","echo ridge","elwynn","kobolds","mcbride","northshire","vineyards","willem"},["n"]="Northshire Valley",["s"]="Tucked away in the northern mountains of Elwynn Forest, Northshire Valley serves as the peaceful cradle and training ground for the kingdom of Stormwind's newest defenders. Surrounded by natural barriers, it hosts the historic Northshire Abbey, fertile vineyards, and the rich Echo Ridge Mine. Despite its tranquil appearance, the valley faces mounting unrest from rogue bandits, infesting kobolds, and displaced predators.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Northshire Valley is framed by nearly impassable mountain ridges, with its only road heading south through a fortified gatehouse toward Goldshire and the rest of Elwynn Forest. A clear river winds through its pastures before feeding south into Crystal Lake. At the valley's heart stands Northshire Abbey, an ancient sanctuary where the Holy Light is taught and where recruits are trained by the Knights of the Silver Hand and seasoned veterans. Beyond the abbey walls lie the bountiful Northshire Vineyards and Echo Ridge Mine, forming a self-sustaining pocket of Stormwind territory that feels far removed from the wider world's wars.",["t"]="A Secluded Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Even this sheltered haven has felt the strain of Stormwind's overextended defenses. Marshal McBride and his detachment of the Stormwind Guard struggle to maintain order across the vale. Packs of wolves driven north from blighted Duskwood prowl the surrounding woods, while vermin-like kobolds have overrun the tunnels of Echo Ridge Mine. Worse still, masked thugs aligned with the Defias Brotherhood openly harass the vineyards and threaten the abbey's grounds, forcing local commanders to recruit every able-bodied civilian arriving at their gates.",["t"]="Encroaching Troubles"}}}}}
t["subzone:northshire-vineyards"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,269,19.577.0,48.206.0,59.276.0,21.227.0",["h"]="73873d",["n"]="Viñedos de Villanorte",["s"]="Viñedos de Villanorte. Los Viñedos de Villanorte son campos de uva cultivados situados justo al este de la Abadía de Villanorte, en la cuenca resguardada del valle. Aunque antaño fueron una pacífica fuente de vino para los clérigos, los campos han caído bajo el control de la Hermandad Defias y sus bandidos locales. Ubicados al este, cruzando el arroyo desde la Abadía de Villanorte, los Viñedos de Villanorte representan la tranquila vida agraria del valle. Los campos son atendidos por trabajadores locales como Milly Osworth, pero la creciente agitación civil los ha dejado desprotegidos. Bandidos alineados con la Hermandad Defias, liderados sobre el terreno por un degollador llamado Garrick Padfoot, se han apoderado de las tierras. Lejos de tratarse de simple vandalismo, los ladrones ocupan los campos para saquear la cosecha y despojar a los granjeros locales de su sustento, proporcionando a los nuevos reclutas de la Hermandad un punto de apoyo fácil justo bajo las narices de la abadía.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The unrest in these peaceful grape fields demonstrates how deeply lawlessness has penetrated even the most protected corners of the kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="For many young humans venturing out into the world, the occupied vineyards are their first direct encounter with the bitterness and reach of the Defias Brotherhood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thieves and cutthroats belonging to the Defias Brotherhood occupy the fields. Their local ringleader is Garrick Padfoot, a wanted rogue who directs the looting of the crops and terrorizes the local workers.",["al"]={"who is at the vineyards","who took over northshire vineyards","who is garrick padfoot"},["q"]="Who controls the Northshire Vineyards right now?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's military resources are stretched extraordinarily thin with King Varian Wrynn missing. The abbey guards have pulled back to defend the abbey itself and watch the valley roads, forcing local farmers to rely on newly arrived adventurers to reclaim their stolen goods.",["al"]={"why no stormwind guards","why isn't the abbey defending the vineyards"},["q"]="Why is the abbey letting bandits run rampant in the fields?"},{["a"]="Milly Osworth is a local farmer working the vineyards. When the Defias bandits moved in and seized the grape harvest, she was driven off and now seeks brave travelers to venture into the fields and recover her plundered crates.",["al"]={"milly osworth","who is milly"},["q"]="Who is Milly Osworth?"}},["kw"]={"defias","elwynn","garrick padfoot","grapes","milly osworth","northshire valley","northshire vineyards"},["n"]="Northshire Vineyards",["s"]="The Northshire Vineyards are cultivated grape fields lying just east of Northshire Abbey in the valley's sheltered basin. Though once a peaceful source of wine for the clerics, the fields have fallen under the control of the Defias Brotherhood and their local brigands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located east across the stream from Northshire Abbey, the Northshire Vineyards represent the valley's quiet agrarian life. The fields are tended by local workers like Milly Osworth, but rising civil unrest has left them unprotected. Bandits aligned with the Defias Brotherhood, led on the ground by a cutthroat named Garrick Padfoot, have seized the acreage. Rather than mere vandalism, the thieves occupy the fields to plunder the harvest and strip the local farmers of their livelihood, providing new recruits to the Brotherhood an easy foothold right under the abbey's nose.",["t"]="A Plundered Harvest"}}}}}
t["subzone:old-town"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,373,26.585.0,28.556.0,66.262.0,37.217.0,48.237.0,32.200.0",["h"]="5b55b8",["n"]="Casco Antiguo",["s"]="Casco Antiguo. Casco Antiguo es el barrio más antiguo y descuidado de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, habiendo sobrevivido en gran parte intacto a la destrucción de la Primera Guerra. En lugar de relucientes plazas de piedra, sus estrechos callejones presentan ladrillos desgastados, viviendas obreras y bulliciosas instalaciones militares. Sirve de hogar para el Centro de Mando militar del reino, así como para el cuartel general clandestino de la organización IV:7. Mientras que el resto de Ventormenta fue meticulosamente reconstruido desde los cimientos por los Albañiles tras la Primera Guerra, Casco Antiguo escapó de la ruina total. Al no haber necesitado una reconstrucción integral, nunca recibió las inmaculadas fachadas de mármol ni los grandes canales presentes en el Distrito de Mercaderes o en la Plaza de la Catedral. Por contra, sigue siendo un barrio rústico y concurrido donde residen trabajadores, peones y los habitantes más humildes de la ciudad. Sus calles adoquinadas son más estrechas, sucias y mucho más caóticas que las del resto de la capital, pero aún conservan la atmósfera auténtica de Ventormenta previa a la guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Old Town is your natural sanctuary in the capital; behind its ordinary alleys lies the headquarters of SI:7, where master spies and covert handlers offer guidance.",["class:Warrior"]="The Command Center and Champions' Hall make Old Town the premier gathering place in Stormwind for battle-tested veterans seeking gear and combat training."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Old Town largely survived the Horde's razing of Stormwind during the First War. Because it was not leveled, the Stonemasons did not rebuild it from scratch, meaning it missed out on the pristine new masonry and grand architecture granted to the rest of the city.",["al"]={"why is old town run down","old town poverty","why is old town gross"},["q"]="Why does Old Town look so much dirtier than the rest of Stormwind?"},{["a"]="SI:7 is the secretive intelligence agency of Stormwind and the Alliance, overseen by Master Mathias Shaw. Their covert headquarters is tucked away in the back of Old Town, past the training yards and military stables.",["al"]={"si7 location","what is si:7","stormwind spies"},["q"]="What is SI:7 and where is it located?"},{["a"]="The Command Center serves as the primary garrison and headquarters for Stormwind's military. Inside and around its yard, officers coordinate city defenses, while warriors and hunters train alongside stable masters and riding instructors.",["al"]={"command center purpose","old town barracks","stormwind military headquarters"},["q"]="What is the Command Center in Old Town used for?"},{["a"]="The local watering hole is the Pig and Whistle Tavern, located near the center of the district. It is famous for hosting hungry soldiers, adventurers, and travelers looking for hearty cooking recipes.",["al"]={"old town inn","pig and whistle location","where is pig and whistle"},["q"]="Where is the tavern in Old Town?"}},["kw"]={"champions hall","command center","first war","mathias shaw","old town","pig and whistle","si:7","stormwind"},["n"]="Old Town",["s"]="Old Town is the oldest and grittiest quarter of Stormwind City, having largely survived the destruction of the First War intact. Rather than gleaming stone plazas, its narrow alleys feature weathered brick, working-class tenements, and bustling military facilities. It serves as home to the kingdom's military Command Center as well as the clandestine headquarters of SI:7.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the rest of Stormwind was painstakingly rebuilt from the ground up by the Stonemasons following the First War, Old Town escaped total ruin. Because it did not require wholesale reconstruction, it never received the pristine marble facades and grand canals seen in the Trade District or Cathedral Square. Instead, it remains a rustic, crowded quarter where working folk, laborers, and the city's poorest residents reside. Its cobbled streets are narrower, dirtier, and far more chaotic than the rest of the capital, yet they preserve the authentic atmosphere of pre-war Stormwind.",["t"]="A Relic of the Old Kingdom"},{["b"]="Behind its weathered tenements, Old Town functions as the martial backbone of the Alliance capital. The Command Center houses Stormwind's military officers, barracks, and combat trainers, alongside the Champions' Hall where the Alliance's finest warriors gather. Tucked away toward the district's edge sits the covert compound of SI:7, the kingdom's secretive intelligence agency led by Master Mathias Shaw. Off-duty footmen and shadowy operatives alike gather at the Pig and Whistle Tavern, rubbing shoulders in one of the city's liveliest watering holes.",["t"]="Soldiers, Spies, and Taverns"}}}}}
t["subzone:olsen-s-farthing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,270,20.455.0,22.434.1,47.192.0,37.190.0,23.163.0,50.150.0",["h"]="5125aa",["n"]="Finca de Olsen",["s"]="Finca de Olsen. La Finca de Olsen fue antaño una próspera granja situada a lo largo del principal camino comercial que atraviesa el Bosque de Argénteos. Tras la Tercera Guerra, los campos quedaron en ruinas y fueron invadidos por siervos reanimados vinculados al nigromante renegado Thule Corvozarpa. Antes de que la plaga consumiera Lordaeron, la Finca de Olsen era una concurrida hacienda agrícola con acceso directo a la principal ruta comercial terrestre del Bosque de Argénteos. Hoy en día, sus campos arados están asfixiados por la maleza, sus estructuras yacen derruidas y cualquier recuerdo de la agricultura honrada ha sido borrado por la nigromancia de la Plaga. Siervos no-muertos, subyugados como esclavos y asaltantes bajo las órdenes de Thule Corvozarpa, deambulan por las tierras yermas para masacrar a cualquier viajero que se acerque demasiado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the raiders from Olsen's Farthing is vital for securing the supply road linking the Sepulcher to the north and the road toward Tirisfal Glades.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, places like Olsen's Farthing are grim reminders of the lingering Scourge threat that seeks to enslave the dead rather than liberate them."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It was a productive roadside farmstead supporting local commerce along Silverpine Forest's main trade thoroughfare, feeding the settlements of Lordaeron before the kingdom fell to the Scourge.",["al"]={"olsens farthing history","what was this place","who lived at olsens farthing"},["q"]="What was Olsen's Farthing before the Third War?"},{["a"]="The farm was destroyed during the Third War and its remnants were seized by the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, who raised the dead as thralls and raiders to terrorize travelers along the road.",["al"]={"why are there undead here","who controls the undead at olsens farthing","ravenclaw slaves silverpine"},["q"]="Why is the farm infested with undead?"},{["a"]="Thule Ravenclaw is a dangerous necromancer aligned with the Scourge who orchestrates undead incursions across Silverpine Forest from his stronghold on Fenris Isle.",["al"]={"who is thule ravenclaw","thule ravenclaw lore","who commands ravenclaw raiders"},["q"]="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?"},{["a"]="No. The farm is completely overrun by hostile undead loyal to Thule Ravenclaw, making it hostile ground for Forsaken scouts and Horde travelers alike.",["al"]={"is olsens farthing horde","do forsaken live at olsens farthing","is there a quest hub here"},["q"]="Does the Horde or Forsaken hold any presence here?"}},["kw"]={"fenris isle","lordaeron farm","olsen's farthing","olsens farthing","ravenclaw raiders","ravenclaw slaves","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},["n"]="Olsen's Farthing",["s"]="Olsen's Farthing was once a flourishing farmstead situated along the primary trade road running through Silverpine Forest. In the wake of the Third War, the fields fell into ruin and became overrun by reanimated thralls bound to the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, Olsen's Farthing was a busy agricultural homestead with direct access to Silverpine's main overland trading route. Today, its tilled fields are choked with weeds, its structures lie broken, and any memory of honest farming has been erased by Scourge necromancy. Undead thralls, bound as slaves and raiders under the command of Thule Ravenclaw, wander the barren grounds to slaughter any travelers who stray too close.",["t"]="A Blighted Homestead"},{["b"]="The shambling horrors haunting Olsen's Farthing are not mindless wanderers, but servants answering to Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful necromancer operating from Fenris Isle in the center of Lake Lordamere. Using dark sorcery to animate and enslave the dead of the surrounding countryside, Thule's reach extends through Olsen's Farthing and poses a direct threat to the Forsaken seeking to secure the northern reaches of Silverpine Forest.",["t"]="The Grasp of Ravenclaw"}}}}}
t["subzone:oracle-glade"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,297,21.596.0,16.473.0,24.279.0,43.245.0,53.253.0,34.178.0",["h"]="daa87b",["n"]="El Claro del Oráculo",["s"]="El Claro del Oráculo. Enclavado en el noroeste de Teldrassil, El Claro del Oráculo es un santuario boscoso sagrado que alberga el portentoso Árbol del Oráculo y la poza de la luna principal del Árbol del Mundo. A pesar de su sereno propósito como centro de comunión y vigilancia, el claro sufre el constante hostigamiento de las invasoras arpías Plumapena. El Claro del Oráculo reposa tranquilamente entre Darnassus y Lago Primigenio, actuando como un nexo vital para la comunión de los elfos de la noche con la naturaleza. En su centro se alza el Árbol del Oráculo, un antiguo espécimen cuyas enormes ramas evocan la silueta de un águila posada sobre un oso. Cerca de allí resplandece la primera y más potente de las pozas de la luna sagradas de Teldrassil, un oasis de magia lunar bañado en La Gracia de Elune. Junto con el Círculo de los Ancestros, el Árbol del Oráculo vela por las ramas de la isla, desprendiendo Corteza grabada que sirve como vitales comunicados para el archidruida Fandral Corzocelada sobre la salud del Árbol del Mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the wild, the Oracle Tree is a living partner in stewardship, offering written records of the land's health shed directly from its very bark.",["race:NightElf"]="The Oracle Glade represents the tender care required to nurse Teldrassil to fruition, housing the crown's most potent moonwell and a silent watcher that speaks directly to the Cenarion leadership."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Oracle Tree is an ancient, magically nurtured tree shaped like a great eagle resting upon a bear. It monitors the growth and health of Teldrassil, shedding inscribed bark containing detailed reports that the druids deliver directly to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",["al"]={"who is the oracle tree","oracle tree lore","talking tree teldrassil"},["q"]="What is the Oracle Tree?"},{["a"]="The Bloodfeather clan of harpies has nested in the high canopies of the glade, drawn by its untamed wilderness and magical vitality. They violently defend their roosts and harass the Oracle Tree, requiring local Sentinels to keep them contained.",["al"]={"bloodfeather harpies","why harpies here","oracle glade enemies"},["q"]="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?"},{["a"]="The pool in the Oracle Glade is the very first and most powerful moonwell established on Teldrassil. It channels the sacred energies of Elune to nourish the surrounding forest and sustain kaldorei druids and priestesses who come to draw upon its waters.",["al"]={"oracle glade moonwell","first moonwell","teldrassil first moonwell"},["q"]="What is the importance of the moonwell in this glade?"},{["a"]="It is located in northwestern Teldrassil, just west of Wellspring Lake. A southern road connects the glade directly back to the main path circling outside the gates of Darnassus.",["al"]={"oracle glade location","where is oracle glade","how to get to oracle glade"},["q"]="Where is the Oracle Glade located?"}},["kw"]={"bloodfeather","fandral staghelm","harpies","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},["n"]="Oracle Glade",["s"]="Nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, the Oracle Glade is a sacred woodland sanctuary home to the wondrous Oracle Tree and the World Tree's premier moonwell. Despite its serene purpose as a center of communion and vigilance, the glade faces constant harassment from encroaching Bloodfeather harpies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Oracle Glade rests quietly between Darnassus and Wellspring Lake, serving as a vital nexus of night elven communion with nature. At its center stands the Oracle Tree, an ancient specimen whose massive boughs evoke the silhouette of an eagle perched atop a bear. Nearby shimmers the first and most potent of Teldrassil's sacred moonwells, an oasis of lunar magic bathed in Elune's grace. Alongside the Circle of the Ancients, the Oracle Tree watches over the island boughs, shedding inscribed bark that acts as vital communiques to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm regarding the World Tree's health.",["t"]="Heart of the Woodland"},{["b"]="The glade's tranquility is fragile. Aggressive Bloodfeather harpies have descended upon the grove, establishing roosts among the high branches and threatening the sacred tree. Sentinels dispatched from Darnassus struggle to root out the avian scavengers, who actively harass traveling druids and taint the natural serenity of the moonwell. Travelers passing through the northern boughs must tread lightly, as the harpies strike swiftly at any who venture near their roosts.",["t"]="A Bough Besieged"}}}}}
t["subzone:palemane-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,242,18.449.0,22.113.0,27.172.0,44.172.0",["h"]="375c68",["n"]="Roca Crines Pálidas",["s"]="Roca Crines Pálidas. Roca Crines Pálidas es una caverna y campamento enclavado en las montañas occidentales de Mulgore. Sirve como bastión principal para la agresiva tribu de gnolls Crines Pálidas, lo que supone una molestia constante y una amenaza para los tauren cercanos de Poblado Pezuña de Sangre. Situada a lo largo del linde occidental de las llanuras cubiertas de hierba de Mulgore, Roca Crines Pálidas consta de un extenso campamento al aire libre frente a una profunda y sombría caverna excavada en la ladera de la montaña. Los gnolls Crines Pálidas han reclamado como territorio propio tanto el interior de la cueva como las colinas circundantes. Hostiles y territoriales, estos gnolls defienden agresivamente su guarida, atacando a cazadores, viajeros y exploradores que se acercan demasiado a su refugio rocoso.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing Mulgore's borders against local pests like the Palemane gnolls is essential for keeping the tauren homeland safe and stable.",["race:Tauren"]="The Palemane gnolls entrenched in these western caves are a persistent thorn in the side of your people, threatening game and unwary wanderers across Mulgore's pastures."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Palemane Rock is a natural cave formation and entrenched gnoll settlement set into the western cliffs of Mulgore.",["al"]={"palemane rock info","palemane cave","where is palemane rock"},["q"]="What is Palemane Rock?"},{["a"]="The cavern and surrounding camp are held by gnolls belonging to the Palemane tribe. They aggressively defend their territory against outsiders, including the native tauren.",["al"]={"who is here","palemane mobs","gnolls at palemane rock"},["q"]="Who lives at Palemane Rock?"},{["a"]="The proximity of Palemane Rock to central Mulgore and Bloodhoof Village makes it an active nest of hostile raiders that tauren hunters and braves must continually suppress.",["al"]={"why do tauren care","bloodhoof village gnolls","threat to mulgore"},["q"]="Why does Palemane Rock matter to the tauren?"}},["kw"]={"bloodhoof","cave","gnoll","mulgore","palemane","rock"},["n"]="Palemane Rock",["s"]="Palemane Rock is a cavern and campsite nestled into the western mountains of Mulgore. It serves as a primary stronghold for the aggressive Palemane gnoll tribe, posing a continual nuisance and threat to the nearby tauren of Bloodhoof Village.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated along the western rim of the grassy plains of Mulgore, Palemane Rock consists of a sprawling open-air encampment fronting a deep, shadowed cavern carved into the mountainside. The Palemane gnolls have claimed both the cave interior and the immediate foothills outside as their territory. Hostile and territorial, these gnolls aggressively defend their den, attacking hunters, travelers, and scouts who wander too close to their rocky haven.",["t"]="A Gnoll Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:park"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="4,338,28.525.0,24.376.0,39.170.0,46.264.0,33.196.0,51.186.0",["h"]="87254d",["n"]="Parque",["s"]="Parque. Enclavado en el extremo occidental de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, entre Plaza de la Catedral y el Barrio de los Magos, el Parque es un frondoso santuario de vegetación y tranquila reflexión. Dedicado a la naturaleza y al ocio en medio de la bulliciosa capital de piedra, sirve como refugio principal para los elfos de la noche que están de visita y alberga a los únicos instructores de druidas de los Reinos del Este. Mientras que el resto de Ventormenta está dominado por paseos empedrados, imponentes murallas de piedra caliza y concurridos puestos de mercado, el Parque ofrece un respiro tranquilo de naturaleza virgen. Establecido originalmente como un apacible lugar de recreo para los habitantes de la ciudad, se transformó de forma natural en un enclave para los emisarios y viajeros elfos de la noche que llegaban desde el otro lado del Mare Magnum. Al abrigo de frondosas copas y alrededor de un Pozo de la Luna central, el distrito trae una pizca de los claros sagrados de Kalimdor al corazón del reino humano.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="This tranquil enclave is your sole sanctuary for training and counsel across all of the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves traveling across the sea, the Park provides a welcome taste of home, centered around a glowing Moonwell and familiar teachers of Elune and the wild."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Park sits along the far western edge of Stormwind City. You can reach its verdant paths by heading southwest from Cathedral Square or northwest from the Mage Quarter.",["al"]={"where is the park","how to get to the park","park location"},["q"]="Where is the Park located in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="The Park was embraced as a refuge by visiting night elves who sought relief from Stormwind's towering stone streets. Its lush groves and serene atmosphere reminded them of their home forests, leading them to settle here and even establish a Moonwell in the square.",["al"]={"why night elves here","stormwind night elf district","kaldorei district"},["q"]="Why are there so many night elves in the Park?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Park is currently the only place anywhere in the Eastern Kingdoms where Alliance druid trainers are stationed, offering guidance and training to Kaldorei practitioners away from Kalimdor.",["al"]={"druid trainers stormwind","where to train druid eastern kingdoms","park druid training"},["q"]="Can I train druid abilities here?"},{["a"]="The pool in the middle of the Park is a consecrated night elven Moonwell, created by Kaldorei visitors to serve as a sacred font of spiritual peace and lunar power amidst the human city.",["al"]={"park moonwell","glowing fountain park","pool in the park"},["q"]="What is the glowing pool in the center of the Park?"}},["kw"]={"druid","kaldorei","moonwell","nara meideros","night elf","park","stormwind"},["n"]="Park",["s"]="Tucked along the western edge of Stormwind City between Cathedral Square and the Mage Quarter, the Park is a lush sanctuary of greenery and quiet reflection. Devoted to nature and leisure amidst the bustling stone capital, it serves as the primary haven for visiting night elves and houses the only druid trainers in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the rest of Stormwind is dominated by cobbled walkways, towering limestone ramparts, and crowded market stalls, the Park offers a tranquil breath of wilderness. Originally established as a quiet place of recreation for the city's populace, it naturally transformed into an enclave for night elf emissaries and travelers arriving from across the Great Sea. Sheltered beneath shaded canopies and surrounding a central Moonwell, the district brings a sliver of Kalimdor's sacred glades into the heart of the human kingdom.",["t"]="A Grove in the Stone Capital"},{["b"]="For the night elves, the Park is a vital foothold in foreign lands. Here, Kaldorei priests such as Nara Meideros tend to visiting pilgrims, and druidic mentors offer their guidance to those devoted to the wild. The district also serves as a peaceful retreat where weary adventurers rest their eyes from the clatter of the Trade District and the solemn duties of the Cathedral.",["t"]="Sanctuary and Fellowship"}}}}}
t["subzone:petitioner-s-chamber"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,373,31.524.0,42.151.0,25.219.0,46.222.0,37.226.0",["h"]="453847",["n"]="cámara de peticiones",["s"]="cámara de peticiones. La cámara de peticiones, también conocida como la Sala de los Peticionarios, es una antecámara situada justo al lado de la rampa de entrada principal del Castillo de Ventormenta. Sirve como sala de espera oficial para la nobleza, los dignatarios de la iglesia y los súbditos visitantes que solicitan una audiencia con la corona. Quienes esperan aquí a menudo pasan las horas relacionándose, bebiendo o aguardando la disposición del regente. Ubicada inmediatamente a la derecha al subir hacia el Castillo de Ventormenta, la cámara de peticiones es donde los asuntos de estado se topan con la burocracia cotidiana. Nobles como el Conde Remington Bonacresta y miembros del clero de alto rango como el Obispo DeLavey pasan el tiempo en estas salas mientras esperan una audiencia con el joven rey Anduin Wrynn y el Alto Señor Bolvar Fordragón. Tras la pulida fachada de la etiqueta cortesana, es un rincón ideal del castillo para los cotilleos, las discretas maniobras de influencia y para discernir quién ostenta verdaderamente el poder en el reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="With Bishop DeLavey often stationed in this antechamber, the room serves as an intersection between the Holy Light's administrative hierarchy and the royal court.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance loyalists, this chamber represents the administrative bottleneck of Stormwind, where domestic appeals, church affairs, and noble requests await the royal council's scarce attention."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The chamber is located inside Stormwind Keep. As soon as you ascend the grand entrance ramp into the keep, it is the first room directly on your right.",["al"]={"where is petitioners chamber","how to find petitioner chamber","petitioner room location"},["q"]="Where is the Petitioner's Chamber located?"},{["a"]="The room is frequented by petitioners, court attendees, and nobles seeking the ear of the throne, including figures like Count Remington Ridgewell, Caledra Dawnbreeze, and Bishop DeLavey of the Church of the Holy Light.",["al"]={"who is in petitioners chamber","npcs in petitioner chamber","who waits here"},["q"]="Who gathers in this room?"},{["a"]="Its formal function is to host subjects who have submitted formal petitions to the crown. Visitors must wait here until the regent, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon, or the royal council grants them admittance to the throne room.",["al"]={"hall of petitioners","why called hall of petitioners","petitioners hall"},["q"]="Why is it also called the Hall of Petitioners?"},{["a"]="The chamber is primarily visited when delivering goods or speaking with nobles and clergy stationed within the keep, such as running errands to supply refined drinks like port for thirsty aristocrats waiting on court business.",["al"]={"petitioner chamber quests","what quests lead here"},["q"]="What happens here during city quests?"}},["kw"]={"bishop delavey","caledra dawnbreeze","count remington ridgewell","hall of petitioners","petitioners chamber","stormwind keep"},["n"]="Petitioner's Chamber",["s"]="The Petitioner's Chamber, also known as the Hall of Petitioners, is an antechamber situated just off the main entrance ramp of Stormwind Keep. It serves as an official waiting room for nobility, church dignitaries, and visiting subjects seeking an audience with the crown. Those lingering here often pass the hours mingling, drinking, or waiting upon the regent's pleasure.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Found immediately to the right upon ascending into Stormwind Keep, the Petitioner's Chamber is where matters of state meet everyday bureaucracy. Nobles such as Count Remington Ridgewell and high-ranking clergy like Bishop DeLavey pass their time in these halls while waiting for an audience with the boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Behind the polished veneer of courtly etiquette, it is an ideal corner of the castle for gossip, quiet lobbying, and discerning who truly holds influence within the realm.",["t"]="A Room of Waiting and Influence"}}}}}
t["subzone:pool-of-ask-ar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,275,27.526.0,27.525.0,27.158.0,36.192.0,37.194.0,44.152.0",["h"]="7f4eb3",["n"]="Alberca de Ask'ar",["s"]="Alberca de Ask'ar. La Alberca de Ask'ar es un extenso lago cavernoso sumergido situado en las profundidades de Cavernas de Brazanegra. Rebosante de bestias acuáticas y viles invasores naga, sus aguas ocultan una antigua arquitectura de elfos de la noche junto a pasadizos ocultos que serpentean más profundamente en el santuario corrompido. Situada justo más allá del Sagrario Inundado, la Alberca de Ask'ar llena una enorme bóveda subterránea con agua turbia y fría. Las cavernas naturales y la antigua cantería se han convertido en un lugar de anidación para tortugas mordedoras descomunales y cangrejos de aguas profundas, vigilados por el enorme y ancestral quelonio conocido como Ghamoo-ra. Los naga que se han apoderado del templo utilizan este umbral sumergido como punto de despliegue defensivo, custodiando los accesos inundados que conducen más hacia el interior del complejo, en dirección a Lady Sarevess y las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The waterways must be breached to uncover the fate of Argent Guard Thaelrid, who ventured into these cavern depths on a holy mission against the Twilight's Hammer.",["race:NightElf"]="The pool floods what was once holy Elune temple grounds, drowning ancient architecture and scattering sacred relics like the Lorgalis Manuscript to be scavenged by naga."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a vast subterranean pool within Blackfathom Deeps, located right past the Drowned Sacellum. It is dominated by snapping turtles, crabs, and naga guards.",["al"]={"pool of askar","what is this pool","bfd water area"},["q"]="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?"},{["a"]="The cavern is inhabited by wild reef creatures such as snapping turtles and crabs, most notably the colossal turtle Ghamoo-ra. Hostile naga also patrol the submerged banks and nearby chambers.",["al"]={"pool monsters","pool of askar bosses","who is in the pool"},["q"]="Who lives in this subterranean pool?"},{["a"]="Navigating the flooded southern passages leads out toward chambers occupied by Lady Sarevess and Argent Guard Thaelrid, and opens into the path winding past Gelihast toward the Moonshrine Ruins.",["al"]={"pool tunnels","where does the water go","pool of askar exit"},["q"]="Where do the underwater tunnels lead?"},{["a"]="The submerged ruins along the pool's periphery contain the Lorgalis Manuscript, an ancient text on the Old Gods coveted by Gerrig Bonegrip of Ironforge.",["al"]={"pool of askar relics","lorgalis manuscript","pool loot"},["q"]="What notable items can be found in the pool?"}},["kw"]={"blackfathom deeps","drowned sacellum","ghamoo-ra","lady sarevess","lorgalis manuscript","naga","pool of ask'ar"},["n"]="Pool of Ask'ar",["s"]="The Pool of Ask'ar is a sprawling, submerged cavern lake located deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Teeming with aquatic beasts and foul naga invaders, its waters conceal ancient night elven architecture alongside hidden passageways that wind deeper into the corrupted sanctuary.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated just beyond the Drowned Sacellum, the Pool of Ask'ar fills a massive subterranean vault with murky, cold water. The natural caverns and ancient stonework have become a nesting ground for oversized snapping turtles and deep-sea crabs, overseen by the enormous ancient chelonian known as Ghamoo-ra. The naga who have taken over the temple utilize this submerged threshold as a defensive staging ground, guarding the waterlogged approaches that lead deeper into the complex toward Lady Sarevess and the Moonshrine Ruins.",["t"]="Depths of the Sunken Grotto"},{["b"]="Beyond its monstrous fauna and hostile patrols, the waters of the pool hide valuable relics from the shrine's pre-Sundering past. Submerged ledges and hidden alcoves along the cavern's edges conceal lost artifacts, including the valuable Lorgalis Manuscript sought by the dwarven scholar Gerrig Bonegrip of Ironforge. Swimming through the flooded southern passageways brings travelers out into dry tunnels guarded by vile murlocs and Old God cultists, marking the pool as the critical aquatic crossroads of Blackfathom Deeps.",["t"]="Secrets Beneath the Surface"}}}}}
t["subzone:pools-of-arlithrien"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,305,20.549.0,42.146.0,36.216.0,45.190.0,62.185.0",["h"]="3a537a",["n"]="Estanques de Arlithrien",["s"]="Estanques de Arlithrien. Los Estanques de Arlithrien son un grupo de manantiales apartados situados en el oeste de Teldrassil, justo al sur de las puertas de Darnassus. Antaño un retiro tranquilo centrado alrededor de una poza de la luna sagrada, la zona ha caído en el abandono y el peligro a medida que la fauna local y los cercanos y hostiles fúrbolgs Tuercepinos la han invadido. Escondidos entre las ramas sombrías al sur de Darnassus, los Estanques de Arlithrien estaban destinados originalmente a ser un lugar tranquilo de armonía natural. En su corazón se encuentra una poza de la luna de piedra, un receptáculo para las aguas imbuidas de la gracia de Elune. Sin embargo, a pesar de su proximidad a la capital de los elfos de la noche, el santuario se ha vuelto peligroso. Bestias agitadas merodean por los bajíos, y la persistente hostilidad de los fúrbolgs Tuercepinos desplazados obligó a los elfos de la noche a abandonar el mantenimiento rutinario del lugar, dejando una maravilla pacífica ensombrecida por el creciente malestar de la isla.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the imbalances of Teldrassil see the unruly wildlife and the neglected moonwell here as another sign that the Great Tree lacks nature's true blessing.",["race:NightElf"]="The abandonment of a holy moonwell so close to Darnassus is a troubling reminder to night elves of the corruption and disruption creeping across Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The pools are nestled in the western reaches of Teldrassil, located just south of the main bridge and entryway into the capital city of Darnassus.",["al"]={"pools of arlithrien location","where is arlithrien","arlithrien map"},["q"]="Where are the Pools of Arlithrien located?"},{["a"]="The night elves withdrew from actively tending the moonwell due to mounting danger. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs established a threatening presence nearby, and aggressive forest wildlife overran the surrounding waters.",["al"]={"why abandoned","arlithrien moonwell abandoned","empty moonwell"},["q"]="Why was the moonwell here abandoned?"},{["a"]="Travelers wandering near the pools must contend with aggressive woodland creatures that have taken over the waters, alongside the looming risk posed by nearby territorial Gnarlpine furbolgs.",["al"]={"arlithrien monsters","pools of arlithrien mobs","enemies at pools"},["q"]="What threats can travelers find at the pools?"},{["a"]="Yes. Though untended and abandoned by the priesthood and druids due to local dangers, the moonwell itself still holds its sacred waters and remains a functional source of lunar essence.",["al"]={"use arlithrien moonwell","is moonwell active","water at pools"},["q"]="Can players still use the moonwell at the Pools of Arlithrien?"}},["kw"]={"arlithrien","darnassus","furbolg","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil"},["n"]="Pools of Arlithrien",["s"]="The Pools of Arlithrien are a cluster of secluded springs resting in western Teldrassil, just south of the gates to Darnassus. Once a tranquil retreat centered around a sacred moonwell, the area has fallen into neglect and danger as local wildlife and nearby hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs encroached upon it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked along the shaded boughs south of Darnassus, the Pools of Arlithrien were originally meant to be a quiet place of natural harmony. At their heart lies a stone moonwell, a vessel for the waters imbued with the grace of Elune. Yet despite its proximity to the night elven capital, the sanctuary has become perilous. Agitated beasts roam the shallows, and the persistent hostility of the displaced Gnarlpine furbolgs forced the night elves to abandon routine upkeep of the site, leaving a peaceful wonder shadowed by the island's growing malaise.",["t"]="A Troubled Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:pools-of-vision"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,238,24.459.0,18.509.0,45.158.0,38.217.0,54.169.0,58.151.0",["h"]="5d169a",["n"]="Pozas de las Visiones",["s"]="Pozas de las Visiones. Las Pozas de las Visiones son una caverna subterránea situada bajo el Alto de los Espíritus, en Cima del Trueno. Marcado por aguas tranquilas y grutas oscuras, este aislado espacio subterráneo sirve como el principal enclave de los Renegados en la capital tauren. Mientras que las cumbres soleadas de Cima del Trueno pertenecen al viento, la tierra y el cielo, las Pozas de las Visiones se adentran directamente bajo el Alto de los Espíritus en un sombrío retiro. Accesible a través de un discreto sendero que parte del puente hacia el alto, esta gruta subterránea ofrece un respiro subterráneo muy diferente a las cabañas al aire libre de arriba. Aquí, las aguas brumosas se estancan en la oscuridad, creando una atmósfera aislada donde los taumaturgos de la Horda se reúnen lejos de las bulliciosas mesetas centrales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The cavern anchors the arcane ley connections to the city; any teleportation spell weaving into Thunder Bluff delivers its caster right beside these secluded pools.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken traversing the plains of Kalimdor, this cavern provides a familiar, shaded haven complete with arcane resources, priestly guidance, and fellowship."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance is a cave mouth located on Spirit Rise, situated immediately to the right just after crossing the wooden rope bridge leading from the lower mesa.",["al"]={"how to get to pools of vision","pools of vision entrance","where are pools of vision"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Pools of Vision?"},{["a"]="The cavern serves as the central hub for Forsaken stationed in Thunder Bluff. It provides shelter away from the harsh Kalimdor sunlight and accommodates practices that may make traditional tauren spiritualists uneasy.",["al"]={"why undead here","why forsaken in cave","thunder bluff undead"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken living down here?"},{["a"]="The cavern hosts trainers and practitioners for priests and mages, along with emissaries for the Defilers who muster soldiers for the war effort in the Arathi Highlands.",["al"]={"trainers in pools of vision","what is in pools of vision","pools of vision trainers"},["q"]="What services can you find inside the Pools of Vision?"},{["a"]="Mages casting a teleport or opening a portal to Thunder Bluff manifest directly inside the sheltered waters of the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise.",["al"]={"mage teleport thunder bluff spot","tb teleport location"},["q"]="Where do mages arrive when they teleport to Thunder Bluff?"}},["kw"]={"defilers","forsaken","mage portal","pools of vision","spirit rise","thunder bluff","undead enclave"},["n"]="Pools of Vision",["s"]="The Pools of Vision are a subterranean cavern nestled beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff. Marked by still waters and dim caverns, this secluded subterranean space serves as the primary enclave for the Forsaken within the tauren capital.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the sunlit peaks of Thunder Bluff belong to the wind, earth, and sky, the Pools of Vision plunge directly beneath Spirit Rise into shadowy seclusion. Accessible from a discreet cave path off the bridge leading to the rise, this subterranean grotto offers subterranean respite quite unlike the open-air lodges above. Here, misty waters pool in the dark, creating an isolated atmosphere where Horde spellcasters gather far from the bustling central mesas.",["t"]="A Haven Beneath the Mesa"},{["b"]="Within Thunder Bluff, the Pools of Vision function as the de facto base of operations for the Forsaken. Travelers from the eastern continent find kindred souls here: undead priests practicing their shadowed arts, mages conjuring arcane portals, and emissaries of the Defilers seeking recruits for their campaigns in the Arathi Highlands. Whether tucked away by tauren skepticism or by the Forsaken's own natural preference for the dark, this quiet refuge bridges Lordaeron's undead with their Kalimdor allies.",["t"]="The Undead Outpost"}}}}}
t["subzone:ragefire-chasm-classic"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="24,324,14.477.0,17.567.1,40.181.0,39.254.0,57.310.0,40.189.0",["h"]="5b233a",["n"]="Sima Ígnea (Classic)",["s"]="Sima Ígnea (Classic). Sima Ígnea es una extensa red de túneles volcánicos excavados directamente bajo Orgrimmar, accesible a través de las profundidades sombrías de El Circo de las Sombras. A pesar de estar situada bajo la capital soberana de la Horda, estas cavernas ardientes están plagadas de hostiles troggs y un aquelarre subversivo de cultistas leales al Consejo de la Sombra. Bajo las calles de piedra y las torres fortificadas de Orgrimmar se encuentra Sima Ígnea, una traicionera red de cavernas subterráneas repletas de magma. Los túneles fueron invadidos recientemente por los salvajes troggs Furia Ígnea, que ascendieron desde profundas fisuras subterráneas. Magatha Tótem Siniestro, de los tauren, intentó una diplomacia pacífica con las criaturas, pero sus propuestas fueron rechazadas violentamente. Si no se les pone freno, los troggs amenazan con excavar aún más en los propios cimientos de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing Ragefire Chasm is a matter of homeland defense, securing the bedrock of Durotar against internal sabotage while rooting out demonic collaborators.",["race:Tauren"]="Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem sent emissaries to sue for peace with the invading troggs; their bloody refusal proved diplomacy is impossible against these underground beasts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance portal is located deep within Orgrimmar, specifically in the subterranean canyon known as the Cleft of Shadow. It sits near the tent of the orc warlock Neeru Fireblade.",["al"]={"where is ragefire","rfc entrance","how to get to rfc","where is rfc located"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="The troggs surfaced from ancient, deep cavern systems beneath Durotar, emerging directly into the volcanic underbelly of the city. Their sudden invasion poses a structural and physical hazard to the capital, refusing any attempts at peaceful containment.",["al"]={"why are troggs here","ragefire troggs","orgrimmar troggs"},["q"]="Why are there troggs beneath Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="Warchief Thrall is fully aware of the cult's presence beneath the city. Rather than launching a blunt assault that might cause the wider network to scatter, he allows them to operate under close watch in hopes they will inadvertently reveal the identity and whereabouts of the Shadow Council's true leadership.",["al"]={"why doesn't thrall clear rfc","thrall shadow council","why is searing blade under orgrimmar"},["q"]="Why does Thrall allow cultists to live under the capital?"},{["a"]="The Searing Blade inside Ragefire Chasm is commanded by three figures: Taragaman the Hungerer, a formidable felguard; Jergosh the Invoker, an orc warlock; and Bazzalan, a treacherous satyr.",["al"]={"rfc bosses","who leads the searing blade","ragefire chasm leaders"},["q"]="Who leads the cultists inside the chasm?"}},["kw"]={"bazzalan","cleft of shadow","jergosh","ragefire chasm","rfc","searing blade","taragaman","troggs"},["n"]="Ragefire Chasm (Classic)",["s"]="Ragefire Chasm is a sprawling network of volcanic tunnels carved directly beneath Orgrimmar, accessible through the shadowy depths of the Cleft of Shadow. Despite being situated under the Horde's sovereign capital, these fiery caverns crawl with hostile troggs and a subversive coven of cultists loyal to the Shadow Council.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Beneath the stone streets and fortified towers of Orgrimmar lies Ragefire Chasm, a treacherous network of magma-filled subterranean caverns. The tunnels recently became overrun by the savage Ragefire troggs, who pushed upward from deep subterranean fissures. Magatha Grimtotem of the tauren attempted peaceful diplomacy with the creatures, but her overtures were violently rejected. Left unchecked, the troggs threaten to tunnel further into the foundations of the city itself.",["t"]="A Hidden Peril"},{["b"]="Far more dangerous than mindless troggs is the presence of the Searing Blade, an insurgent cult subordinate to the demonic Shadow Council. Led by the hulking felguard Taragaman the Hungerer, the orc warlock Jergosh the Invoker, and the corrupt satyr Bazzalan, these conspirators scheme to unravel everything Thrall's Horde has established in Durotar. Rather than immediately cleansing the caves, Warchief Thrall has maintained surveillance on their activities, hoping their foolish overconfidence will expose their masters higher up in the Shadow Council's hierarchy.",["t"]="The Searing Blade"}}}}}
